        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "换新旗"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.banners_new.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition banners_new: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die halbe Sonne behalten"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Keep the half sun"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Conservar el medio sol"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Garder le demi-soleil"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tenere il mezzo sole"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "半分の太陽を残す"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Manter o meio sol"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "留着半轮太阳"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.banners_new.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition banners_new: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sparsamkeit und Respekt. Meine zwei Lieblingswörter, und ausnahmsweise sind sie sich einig. Behaltet die alten."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Thrift and respect. My two favourite words, and for once they agree. Keep the old ones."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ahorro y respeto. Mis dos palabras favoritas, y por una vez están de acuerdo. Conserve los viejos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’économie et le respect. Mes deux mots préférés, et pour une fois, ils sont d’accord. Gardez les anciennes."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Risparmio e rispetto. Le mie due parole preferite, e per una volta vanno d’accordo. Tenete i vecchi."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "倹約と敬意。わたくしの好きな言葉が二つ、珍しく意見が合いました。古いほうで十分です。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Economia e respeito. As minhas duas palavras preferidas, e pela primeira vez estão de acordo. Fique com os antigos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "节俭与敬重。我最爱的两个词，难得意见一致。留着旧的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.banners_new.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition banners_new: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Am Abend hängen die neuen Banner, blaugrün und golden. Pip salutiert jedes Mal, wenn er vorbeigeht, und heimlich tut Ihr es auch."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The new banners go up by evening, teal and gold. Pip salutes them every time he passes, and so, secretly, do you."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al anochecer ya cuelgan los nuevos, verde azulado y oro. Pip los saluda cada vez que pasa, y usted, en secreto, también."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le soir, les nouvelles bannières sont en place, bleu canard et or. Pip les salue chaque fois qu’il passe, et vous aussi, en secret."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Entro sera i nuovi stendardi sono appesi, verde petrolio e oro. Pip li saluta ogni volta che passa, e in segreto lo fate anche voi."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "夕方には新しい旗が掛かる。青緑と金。ピップは前を通るたびに敬礼する。人目を忍んで、あなたも。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os estandartes novos sobem ao entardecer, verde-azulados e dourados. Pip bate continência para eles toda vez que passa, e você também, em segredo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "傍晚时新旗挂了起来，青绿与金。皮普每次经过都要敬个礼，你也悄悄地敬。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.banners_new.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition banners_new: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die alten Banner bleiben. Manche der älteren Wachen nicken ihnen morgens zu, so wie man jemandem zunickt, den man vermisst."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The old banners stay. Some of the older guards nod to them in the morning, the way you nod to someone you miss."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los viejos estandartes se quedan. Algunos de los guardias veteranos los saludan con la cabeza por la mañana, como se saluda a alguien a quien se echa de menos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les vieilles bannières restent. Certains des plus anciens gardes leur font un signe de tête le matin, comme on salue quelqu’un qui vous manque."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I vecchi stendardi restano. Alcune delle guardie più anziane li salutano con un cenno al mattino, come si saluta qualcuno che ci manca."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "古い旗は残る。年かさの衛兵の何人かは、朝、旗に会釈する。会えなくなった誰かに会釈するように。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os estandartes antigos ficam. Alguns dos guardas mais velhos os cumprimentam com a cabeça de manhã, como se cumprimenta alguém de quem se sente falta."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "旧旗留下了。有几个老卫兵早上会朝它们点点头，就像朝一个想念的人点头。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.banners_new.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition banners_new (odile): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mein Herr|Meine Herrin}, die ältesten Banner im Saal zeigen eine halbe Sonne über der Laterne, und die Motten haben das meiste gefressen. Zwanzig Gold für neues Tuch, schlicht blaugrün und gold. Oder wir behalten die alten, aus Respekt und Sparsamkeit."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, the hall’s oldest banners show half a sun above the lantern, and the moths have eaten most of it. Twenty gold buys new cloth, plain teal and gold. Or we keep the old ones, out of respect and thrift."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, los estandartes más antiguos del salón muestran medio sol sobre el farol, y las polillas se han comido casi todo. Veinte monedas de oro compran tela nueva, verde azulado y oro, sin más. O conservamos los viejos, por respeto y por ahorro."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, les plus vieilles bannières de la salle montrent un demi-soleil au-dessus de la lanterne, et les mites en ont mangé la plus grande part. Pour vingt pièces d’or, on aurait une étoffe neuve, bleu canard et or, toute simple. Ou nous gardons les anciennes, par respect et par économie."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, gli stendardi più antichi del salone mostrano un mezzo sole sopra la lanterna, e le tarme se ne sono mangiate quasi tutto. Con venti monete d’oro si compra stoffa nuova, semplice, verde petrolio e oro. Oppure teniamo i vecchi, per rispetto e per risparmio."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、大広間でいちばん古い旗には、ランタンの上に半分の太陽が描かれておりますが、大半は虫に食われてしまいました。金貨20枚で新しい布が買えます。青緑と金だけの、飾りのないものです。それとも敬意と倹約のために、古いものを残しますか。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, os estandartes mais antigos do salão mostram meio sol sobre a lanterna, e as traças comeram quase tudo. Vinte moedas de ouro compram pano novo, verde-azulado e dourado, sem enfeite. Ou ficamos com os antigos, por respeito e economia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "大人，大厅里最老的旗帜上，提灯上方是半轮太阳，大半已被虫蛀了。20金币可以买新布，素净的青绿与金。要么留着旧的，既是敬重，也是节俭。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Für die Stille zahlen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pay for silence"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagar por su silencio"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Payer pour le silence"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagare per il silenzio"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "沈黙を買う"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagar pelo silêncio"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "花钱买清静"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dann singt es eben"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sing it, then"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pues cántela"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chantez-la, alors"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "E allora cantatela"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "なら、歌えばいい"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Então cante"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "那就唱吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An den Pranger mit ihm"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Put him in the stocks"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al cepo con él"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mettez-le au pilori"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mettetelo alla gogna"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "さらし台に掛けてくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ao pelourinho com ele"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "把他锁上枷台"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Einen Erpresser zu bezahlen wird zur Gewohnheit. Ihn auszulachen ist die Heilung. Lasst ihn singen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Paying a blackmailer is a habit. Laughing at him is a cure. Let him sing."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagarle a un chantajista se vuelve costumbre. Reírse de él es la cura. Déjelo cantar."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Payer un maître chanteur devient une habitude. En rire est un remède. Laissez-le chanter."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagare un ricattatore diventa un’abitudine. Ridergli in faccia è la cura. Lasciatelo cantare."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "強請に払えば、癖になります。笑い飛ばせば、治ります。歌わせておけばよいのです。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagar um chantagista vira hábito. Rir dele é a cura. Deixe-o cantar."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "给勒索者付钱，会成习惯。笑他，才能治本。让他唱吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Barde nimmt das Gold und singt ein anderes Lied. Es handelt von {einem Burgherrn, der|einer Burgherrin, die} Barden für Stille bezahlt. Auch das ist beliebt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The bard takes the gold and sings a different song. It is about a {lord|lady} who pays bards for silence. It is also popular."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El bardo toma el oro y canta otra canción. Trata de {un señor|una señora} que paga a los bardos por su silencio. También es popular."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le barde prend l’or et chante une autre chanson. Elle parle {d’un seigneur|d’une dame} qui paie les bardes pour qu’ils se taisent. Elle a aussi du succès."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bardo prende l’oro e canta un’altra canzone. Parla di {un signore|una signora} che paga i bardi per farli tacere. È popolare anche quella."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "吟遊詩人は金を受け取り、別の歌を歌う。吟遊詩人に金を払って黙らせる城主の歌だ。これもまた評判になる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O bardo pega o ouro e canta outra canção. É sobre {um senhor|uma senhora} que paga bardos para ficarem calados. Também faz sucesso."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "诗人收了金币，换唱另一首歌。唱的是一位花钱让诗人闭嘴的城主。这首也很受欢迎。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das tut er. Überall. Ihr hört den Refrain im Saal gepfiffen und einmal, ganz leise, aus Odiles Schreibstube."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He does. Everywhere. You hear the chorus whistled in the hall, and once, faintly, from Odile’s study."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Y la canta. En todas partes. Oye silbar el estribillo en el salón y, una vez, muy bajito, desde el despacho de Odile."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il la chante. Partout. Vous entendez siffler le refrain dans la salle, et une fois, tout bas, dans le cabinet d’Odile."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "E la canta. Ovunque. Sentite fischiettare il ritornello nel salone e una volta, piano piano, dallo studio di Odile."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "彼は歌う。どこででも。大広間では繰り返しの句が口笛で吹かれ、一度など、オディールの書斎からかすかに聞こえてくる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele canta. Em toda parte. Você ouve o refrão assobiado no salão e, uma vez, bem baixinho, vindo do gabinete de Odile."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他唱了。到处都唱。你听见大厅里有人用口哨吹着副歌，有一回，奥黛尔的书房里也隐约传出了这个调子。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Barde singt vom Pranger aus vor mehr Publikum als je zuvor. Manche bringen Kissen mit."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The bard sings from the stocks to a larger crowd than ever. Some of them bring cushions."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El bardo canta desde el cepo ante más público que nunca. Algunos traen cojines."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le barde chante depuis le pilori devant une foule plus nombreuse que jamais. Certains apportent des coussins."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bardo canta dalla gogna davanti a una folla più grande che mai. Qualcuno si porta il cuscino."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "吟遊詩人はさらし台から、かつてない大勢の客に向かって歌う。敷物を持参する者までいる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O bardo canta do pelourinho para uma plateia maior do que nunca. Alguns levam almofadas."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "诗人在枷台上唱，听众比以往任何时候都多。有些人还带了坐垫。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_satire.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition bard_satire (bard, follow-up of bard_song): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}! Ihr erinnert Euch vielleicht an mich. Ich habe ein neues Lied geschrieben: „{Der Burgherr, der|Die Burgherrin, die} nicht zahlen wollte“. Es ist sehr beliebt. Ich könnte natürlich aufhören, es zu singen. Künstler müssen essen. Dreißig Gold kaufen sehr viel Stille."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}! You may remember me. I have written a new song, “The {Lord|Lady} Who Would Not Pay”. It is very popular. I could stop singing it, of course. Artists must eat. Thirty gold buys a great deal of silence."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "¡{Mi señor|Mi señora}! Quizá me recuerde. He escrito una canción nueva: «{El señor|La señora} que no quiso pagar». Es muy popular. Podría dejar de cantarla, claro. Los artistas tienen que comer. Treinta monedas de oro compran muchísimo silencio."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame} ! Vous vous souvenez peut-être de moi. J’ai écrit une nouvelle chanson, « {Le seigneur|La dame} qui ne voulait pas payer ». Elle a beaucoup de succès. Je pourrais cesser de la chanter, bien sûr. Les artistes doivent manger. Trente pièces d’or achètent beaucoup de silence."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}! Forse vi ricordate di me. Ho scritto una nuova canzone, «{Il signore|La signora} che non voleva pagare». È molto popolare. Potrei smettere di cantarla, s’intende. Gli artisti devono mangiare. Trenta monete d’oro comprano parecchio silenzio."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様！　覚えておいでかもしれませんね。新しい歌を作りました。『払わなかった城主様』。たいそうな評判です。もちろん、歌うのをやめることもできます。芸人も食べねばなりません。金貨30枚で、沈黙がたっぷり買えますよ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}! Talvez se lembre de mim. Escrevi uma canção nova, “{O senhor|A senhora} que não quis pagar”. Faz muito sucesso. Eu poderia parar de cantá-la, claro. Artistas precisam comer. Trinta moedas de ouro compram muito silêncio."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人！您也许还记得我。我写了一首新歌，《不肯付钱的城主》。很受欢迎。当然，我也可以不唱。艺术家也得吃饭。30金币，能买来好一阵清静。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.bard_song.c1" : {
