            "value" : "在喉谷门放了它"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.captured_sootling.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition captured_sootling: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Löscht ihn. Wollte die Düsternis, dass wir Haustiere haben, würde sie Kätzchen schicken."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Put it out. If the Gloom wanted us to have pets, it would send kittens."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apáguelo. Si la Penumbra quisiera que tuviéramos mascotas, mandaría gatitos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Éteignez-le. Si la Pénombre voulait que nous ayons des animaux, elle enverrait des chatons."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spegnetelo. Se la Penombra volesse regalarci degli animaletti, ci manderebbe dei gattini."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "消しなさいませ。宵闇が我らに愛玩動物を飼わせたいなら、子猫をよこすでしょう。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apague-o. Se a Penumbra quisesse que tivéssemos bichos de estimação, mandaria gatinhos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "熄了它。暗霭要是想让我们养宠物，就该送小猫来。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.captured_sootling.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition captured_sootling: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hesper hält das Glas an die Flamme, bis das kleine Ding erlischt. Niemand lacht. Pip nimmt die Mütze ab."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hesper holds the jar to the Flame until the small thing goes out. Nobody laughs. Pip takes off his cap."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hesper acerca el frasco a la Llama hasta que la cosita se apaga. Nadie se ríe. Pip se quita el gorro."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hesper tient le bocal contre la Flamme jusqu’à ce que la petite chose s’éteigne. Personne ne rit. Pip ôte son bonnet."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hesper avvicina il barattolo alla Fiamma finché la cosina non si spegne. Nessuno ride. Pip si toglie il berretto."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ヘスパーは瓶を炎にかざし、小さなものが消えるまで待つ。誰も笑わない。ピップが帽子を脱ぐ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hesper segura o pote junto à Chama até a coisinha se apagar. Ninguém ri. Pip tira o gorro."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "赫斯珀把罐子凑到圣焰前，直到那个小东西熄灭。没人笑。皮普摘下了帽子。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.captured_sootling.r2a" : {
      "comment" : "Petition captured_sootling: choice 2, it went well.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bram findet heraus, dass Gerald Eisenspäne hasst. In der Nacht werden die Pfahlgruben damit bestreut, und weniger Rußlinge kommen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bram finds that Gerald hates iron filings. That night the stake pits are dusted with them, and fewer sootlings come."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bram descubre que Gerald odia las limaduras de hierro. Esa noche esparcen limaduras en los fosos de estacas, y vienen menos hollinejos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bram découvre que Gerald déteste la limaille de fer. Cette nuit-là, on en saupoudre les fosses à pieux, et moins de fumerons viennent."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bram scopre che Gerald odia la limatura di ferro. Quella notte le fosse a pali ne vengono cosparse, e arrivano meno fuligginelli."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ブラムが、ジェラルドは鉄くずを嫌うと突き止める。その夜、杭穴に鉄くずがまかれ、来る煤影が減る。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bram descobre que Gerald detesta limalha de ferro. Naquela noite, os fossos de estacas são polvilhados com ela, e vêm menos fuliginhos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "布拉姆发现杰拉尔德讨厌铁屑。那一夜，尖桩坑里撒满了铁屑，来的煤影少了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.captured_sootling.r2b" : {
      "comment" : "Petition captured_sootling: choice 2, it went badly.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Um Mitternacht entkommt Gerald aus dem Glas. Der Nebel ist in dieser Nacht dichter denn je, als suche er nach ihm."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gerald escapes the jar at midnight. The fog that night is thicker than ever, as if it were looking for him."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gerald se escapa del frasco a medianoche. Esa noche la niebla es más espesa que nunca, como si lo buscara."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gerald s’échappe du bocal à minuit. Cette nuit-là, le brouillard est plus épais que jamais, comme s’il le cherchait."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A mezzanotte Gerald scappa dal barattolo. Quella notte la nebbia è più fitta che mai, come se lo cercasse."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "真夜中、ジェラルドが瓶から逃げ出す。その夜の霧は、かつてないほど濃い。ジェラルドを探しているかのように。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gerald escapa do pote à meia-noite. A névoa daquela noite está mais densa do que nunca, como se o procurasse."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "半夜，杰拉尔德逃出了罐子。那一夜的雾比以往都浓，仿佛在找它。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.captured_sootling.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition captured_sootling: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bei Dämmerung wird das Glas am Schlundtor geöffnet. Gerald blickt einmal zum Herdlicht zurück, dann geht er, wohin sie alle gehen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "At dusk the jar is opened at the Throat gate. Gerald looks back once at the hearth light, then goes the way they all go."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al anochecer abren el frasco en la puerta de la Garganta. Gerald mira una vez hacia la luz del hogar, y luego se va por donde se van todos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Au crépuscule, on ouvre le bocal à la porte de la Gorge. Gerald se retourne une fois vers la lumière de l’âtre, puis s’en va par où ils s’en vont tous."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al crepuscolo il barattolo viene aperto alla porta della Gola. Gerald si volta una volta verso la luce del focolare, poi va dove vanno tutti."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "日暮れ、喉谷の門で瓶が開けられる。ジェラルドは一度だけ炉の明かりを振り返り、それから皆が行く方へ去っていく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ao crepúsculo, o pote é aberto no portão da Garganta. Gerald olha uma vez para trás, para a luz da lareira, e depois vai para onde todos eles vão."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "黄昏时，罐子在喉谷门前打开了。杰拉尔德回头望了一眼炉火的光，然后走上了它们都走的那条路。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.captured_sootling.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition captured_sootling (soldier): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Herr|Herrin}! Wir haben einen Rußling in einem Gurkenglas gefangen! Er ist klein und still und hält sich an die Seite, wo der Herd ist. Hesper sagt, löscht ihn. Odile sagt, erforscht ihn. Pip sagt, gebt ihm einen Namen. Er heißt jetzt Gerald. Was machen wir mit Gerald?"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}! We caught a sootling in a pickle jar! It is small and silent and keeps to the side where the hearth is. Hesper says put it out. Odile says study it. Pip says name it. We named it Gerald. What do we do with Gerald?"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "¡{Señor|Señora}! ¡Atrapamos un hollinejo en un frasco de pepinillos! Es pequeño y callado, y se queda del lado donde está el hogar. Hesper dice que lo apaguemos. Odile, que lo estudiemos. Pip, que le pongamos nombre. Se llama Gerald. ¿Qué hacemos con Gerald?"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame} ! On a attrapé un fumeron dans un bocal à cornichons ! Il est petit, silencieux, et se tient du côté de l’âtre. Hesper dit de l’éteindre. Odile dit de l’étudier. Pip dit de lui donner un nom. On l’a appelé Gerald. Qu’est-ce qu’on fait de Gerald ?"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Signore|Signora}! Abbiamo preso un fuligginello in un barattolo di sottaceti! È piccolo e silenzioso e sta dalla parte del focolare. Hesper dice di spegnerlo. Odile dice di studiarlo. Pip dice di dargli un nome. L’abbiamo chiamato Gerald. Che facciamo con Gerald?"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主！　漬物の瓶で煤影を一匹捕まえました！　小さくて、音も立てず、炉のある側にばかり寄っています。マザー・ヘスパーは消せと言い、オディール様は調べろと言い、ピップは名前をつけろと言う。それでジェラルドと名づけました。ジェラルドをどうしましょう？"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Senhor|Senhora}! Pegamos um fuliginho num pote de picles! É pequeno e calado e fica do lado em que está a lareira. Hesper diz para apagá-lo. Odile diz para estudá-lo. Pip diz para dar um nome. Demos o nome de Gerald. O que fazemos com Gerald?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主！我们用腌菜罐抓了一只煤影！它很小，一声不出，总贴在靠炉火的那一边。赫斯珀嬷嬷说把它熄了。奥黛尔大人说研究它。皮普说给它起个名字。我们叫它杰拉尔德。杰拉尔德怎么办？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.castle_statue.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition castle_statue: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Meißelt sie"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Carve it"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tállela"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Taillez-la"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Scolpitela"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "彫ってくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pode esculpir"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "雕吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.castle_statue.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition castle_statue: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nehmt die Steine für Mauern"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Use the stone for walls"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Use la piedra para las murallas"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Prenez la pierre pour les murailles"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Usate la pietra per le mura"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "石は城壁に使ってくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Use a pedra nas muralhas"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "石头拿去修墙"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.castle_statue.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition castle_statue: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fünfzehn Gold Brot für eine Statue, die die Stadt lieben und Pip verkleiden wird. Lasst meißeln."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fifteen gold of bread for a statue the town will love and Pip will dress up. Carve it."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quince monedas para pan, a cambio de una estatua que el pueblo adorará y Pip disfrazará. Que la tallen."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quinze pièces d’or de pain pour une statue que la ville aimera et que Pip déguisera. Taillez-la."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quindici monete d’oro di pane per una statua che il borgo amerà e che Pip travestirà. Fatela scolpire."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "町が愛し、ピップが着せ替えたがる像が、金貨15枚分のパンで。彫らせなさいませ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quinze moedas de ouro em pão por uma estátua que a cidade vai amar e Pip vai fantasiar. Mande esculpir."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "15金币的面包，换一座镇上会爱、皮普会给它打扮的石像。雕吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.castle_statue.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition castle_statue: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Binnen einer Woche steht Sankt Taper in Stein am Ende des Burghofs, die Laterne erhoben. Die Nase ist Eure. Nachts hängt Pip eine echte Laterne daran."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In a week Saint Taper stands at the courtyard’s end in stone, lantern raised. The nose is yours. Pip hangs a real lantern on it at night."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "En una semana, san Taper se alza en piedra al fondo del patio de armas, farol en alto. La nariz es la suya. Por las noches, Pip le cuelga un farol de verdad."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "En une semaine, saint Taper se dresse en pierre au bout de la cour, lanterne levée. Le nez est le vôtre. La nuit, Pip y accroche une vraie lanterne."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In una settimana san Taper è in piedi in fondo al cortile, di pietra, la lanterna alzata. Il naso è il vostro. Di notte Pip ci appende una lanterna vera."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一週間で、中庭の奥に石の聖テイパーが立つ。ランタンを掲げて。鼻はあなたのものだ。夜になると、ピップが本物のランタンを掛ける。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Em uma semana, são Taper está de pé no fundo do pátio, em pedra, de lanterna erguida. O nariz é o seu. À noite, Pip pendura nela uma lanterna de verdade."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一周后，圣泰珀的石像立在庭院尽头，高举提灯。鼻子是你的。夜里，皮普往上面挂一盏真的提灯。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.castle_statue.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition castle_statue: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Steinmetze zucken die Schultern und schleppen die Steine zur mittleren Linie. Einer ritzt trotzdem eine winzige Laterne in einen Block."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The masons shrug and haul the stone to the middle line. One of them carves a tiny lantern into a block anyway."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los canteros se encogen de hombros y acarrean la piedra a la línea central. Uno de ellos, de todos modos, talla un farol diminuto en un bloque."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les tailleurs haussent les épaules et traînent la pierre jusqu’à la ligne du milieu. L’un d’eux grave quand même une minuscule lanterne dans un bloc."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gli scalpellini alzano le spalle e trascinano la pietra alla linea di mezzo. Uno di loro incide comunque una minuscola lanterna su un blocco."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "石工たちは肩をすくめ、石を中の防衛線へ運ぶ。それでも一人が、石の一つに小さなランタンを刻む。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os canteiros dão de ombros e levam a pedra para a linha do meio. Mesmo assim, um deles entalha uma lanterninha num bloco."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "石匠们耸耸肩，把石头拖去了中防线。其中一个还是在一块石头上刻了一盏小小的提灯。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.castle_statue.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition castle_statue (builder): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, wir Steinmetze haben Steine von der äußeren Linie übrig. Statuen von Burgherren sind für die Toten und stehen an der Moorstraße. Also: Sankt Taper mit seiner Laterne, für den Burghof, für fünfzehn Gold Brot. Ich nehme Eure Nase."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, we masons have stone left over from the outer line. Statues of lords are for the dead and stand on the moor road. So: Saint Taper with his lantern, for the courtyard, for fifteen gold of bread. I will use your nose."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, a los canteros nos sobró piedra de la línea exterior. Las estatuas de señores son para los muertos y están en el camino del páramo. Así que: san Taper con su farol, para el patio de armas. Nos basta con quince monedas de oro para pan. Usaré su nariz."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, nous, les tailleurs de pierre, avons des pierres en trop de la ligne extérieure. Les statues de seigneurs sont pour les morts et se dressent sur la route de la lande. Alors : saint Taper et sa lanterne, pour la cour, pour quinze pièces d’or de pain. Je prendrai votre nez."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, a noi scalpellini sono avanzate pietre della linea esterna. Le statue dei signori sono per i morti e stanno lungo la strada della brughiera. Quindi: san Taper con la sua lanterna, per il cortile, per quindici monete d’oro di pane. Userò il vostro naso."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、我ら石工のところに、外の防衛線の石が余っております。城主の像は亡き方のためのもので、荒野の道に立つものです。ですので、ランタンを持った聖テイパーを中庭に。お代は、金貨15枚分のパンで結構です。鼻は、城主様のをお借りします。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, nós, canteiros, temos pedra sobrando da linha externa. Estátuas de senhores são para os mortos e ficam na estrada da charneca. Então: são Taper com a lanterna dele, para o pátio, por quinze moedas de ouro em pão. Vou usar o seu nariz."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我们石匠修外防线还剩了些石头。城主的像是给死人立的，都立在荒原之路边上。所以：圣泰珀提着他的提灯，立在庭院里，只要15金币的面包钱。鼻子就照您的雕。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Still und voller Sterne"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quiet, and full of stars"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tranquilas, y llenas de estrellas"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Calmes, et pleines d’étoiles"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Silenziose, e piene di stelle"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "静かで、星がいっぱいだったよ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Era quieto e cheio de estrelas"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "很安静，满天星星"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eines Tages wirst du sie sehen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "One day you will see them"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Algún día las verás"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un jour, tu les verras"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un giorno le vedrai"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "いつか、きっと星が見られるよ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Um dia você vai vê-las"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "总有一天你会看见的"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Daran erinnert sich keiner mehr"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nobody remembers anymore"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ya nadie se acuerda"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Plus personne ne s’en souvient"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nessuno se lo ricorda più"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "もう、誰も覚えていないんだ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ninguém mais se lembra"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "已经没人记得了"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sagt dem Kind die Wahrheit, aber die schöne Hälfte davon."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tell the child the truth, but the nice half of it."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cuéntele la verdad al niño, pero la mitad bonita."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dites la vérité à l’enfant, mais la jolie moitié."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dite al bambino la verità, ma la metà bella."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "本当のことを話しておやりなさいませ。ただし、きれいなほうの半分を。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Conte a verdade à criança, mas a metade bonita."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "跟孩子说实话，但只说好的那一半。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Kind hört mit riesigen Augen zu und rennt dann los, um allen zu erzählen, {der Burgherr|die Burgherrin} habe die Sterne gezählt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The child listens with enormous eyes, then runs off to tell everyone that the {lord|lady} has counted the stars."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El niño escucha con unos ojos enormes y luego sale corriendo a contarle a todo el mundo que {el señor|la señora} ha contado las estrellas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant écoute avec des yeux immenses, puis file raconter à tout le monde que {le seigneur|la dame} a compté les étoiles."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino ascolta con occhi enormi, poi corre a raccontare a tutti che {il signore|la signora} ha contato le stelle."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもは目をまんまるにして聞き入り、それから、城主様は星を数えたことがあるんだって、と皆に触れ回りに駆けていく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A criança escuta com olhos enormes, depois sai correndo para contar a todo mundo que {o senhor|a senhora} contou as estrelas."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子睁大了眼睛听着，然后跑去告诉每一个人，说城主数过星星。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Kind nickt sehr ernst, als hättet Ihr einen Eid geschworen. Vielleicht habt Ihr das."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The child nods very seriously, as if you had sworn an oath. Perhaps you have."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El niño asiente muy serio, como si usted hubiera hecho un juramento. Quizá lo hizo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant hoche la tête très sérieusement, comme si vous aviez prêté serment. Peut-être l’avez-vous fait."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino annuisce, serissimo, come se aveste fatto un giuramento. Forse l’avete fatto."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもはとても真剣にうなずく。まるで誓いを立ててもらったかのように。もしかすると、立てたのかもしれない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A criança assente com muita seriedade, como se você tivesse feito um juramento. Talvez tenha."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子非常认真地点点头，仿佛你立了誓。也许你真的立了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Kind runzelt die Stirn und geht die älteste Frau im Tal fragen, die sich an alles erinnert, und zwar laut."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The child frowns, then goes to ask the oldest woman in the valley, who remembers everything, loudly."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El niño frunce el ceño y luego va a preguntarle a la mujer más vieja del valle, que se acuerda de todo, y en voz alta."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant fronce les sourcils, puis va demander à la plus vieille femme de la vallée, qui se souvient de tout, haut et fort."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino aggrotta la fronte, poi va a chiedere alla donna più vecchia della valle, che si ricorda tutto, ad alta voce."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもは眉を寄せ、それから谷でいちばんの年寄りの女に聞きに行く。何でも覚えていて、それを大声で話す人だ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A criança franze a testa e vai perguntar à mulher mais velha do vale, que se lembra de tudo, em voz alta."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子皱起眉，跑去问河谷里年纪最大的老婆婆。她什么都记得，说起来还特别大声。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.child_question.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition child_question (child, endless only): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, meine Oma sagt, bevor das Leuchtfeuer erlosch, waren die Nächte still, und von der Mauer sah man sein Licht den ganzen Schlund hinunter. Stimmt das? Wie war das? Ich habe immer nur die Feuer gesehen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, my gran says before the beacon went dark the nights were quiet, and from the wall you could see its light all the way down the Throat. Is that true? What was it like? I have only ever seen the fires."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, mi abuela dice que antes de que se apagara la almenara las noches eran tranquilas, y desde la muralla se veía su luz por toda la Garganta. ¿Es verdad? ¿Cómo era? Yo solo he visto los fuegos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, ma mémé dit qu’avant que le fanal s’éteigne, les nuits étaient calmes, et que de la muraille on voyait sa lumière tout au long de la Gorge. C’est vrai ? C’était comment ? Moi, je n’ai jamais vu que les feux."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, mia nonna dice che prima che il faro si spegnesse le notti erano tranquille, e dalle mura si vedeva la sua luce fino in fondo alla Gola. È vero? Com’era? Io ho visto solo i fuochi."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、おばあちゃんが言ってたの。烽火が消える前は夜が静かで、城壁から喉谷の奥までずっと、その光が見えたんだって。本当？　どんなだった？　火しか見たことないもん。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, a minha avó diz que, antes de o farol se apagar, as noites eram quietas, e da muralha dava para ver a luz dele por toda a Garganta. É verdade? Como era? Eu só vi as fogueiras."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我奶奶说，烽火熄灭以前，夜里很安静，站在城墙上能看见它的光一直照到喉谷深处。真的吗？那是什么样子？我只见过那些火堆。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.chronicle.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition chronicle: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
