            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Queime o restolho"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "烧掉麦茬"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vogelscheuchen auf jedes Feld"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Scarecrows on every field"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Espantapájaros en cada campo"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un épouvantail dans chaque champ"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Uno spaventapasseri in ogni campo"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "どの畑にも案山子を"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Espantalhos em todos os campos"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "每块田都立稻草人"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Krähen müssen auch fressen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Crows must eat too"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los cuervos también tienen que comer"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les corneilles aussi doivent manger"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Anche le cornacchie devono mangiare"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "烏も食べねばならない"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Corvo também precisa comer"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "鸦也得吃东西"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Verbrannte Stoppeln sind der Hunger von morgen. Vogelscheuchen kosten Stroh und ein wenig Stolz. Vogelscheuchen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Burnt stubble is next year’s hunger. Scarecrows cost straw and a little pride. Scarecrows."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El rastrojo quemado es el hambre del año que viene. Los espantapájaros cuestan paja y un poco de orgullo. Espantapájaros."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le chaume brûlé, c’est la faim de l’an prochain. Les épouvantails coûtent de la paille et un peu de fierté. Les épouvantails."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le stoppie bruciate sono la fame dell’anno prossimo. Gli spaventapasseri costano paglia e un po’ d’orgoglio. Spaventapasseri."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "刈り株を焼けば、来年の飢えです。案山子なら、藁と少しの誇りで済みます。案山子を。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Restolho queimado é a fome do ano que vem. Espantalhos custam palha e um pouco de orgulho. Espantalhos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "烧掉的麦茬，就是来年的饥荒。稻草人只费些稻草，再丢点面子。稻草人。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Rauch treibt die Krähen in den Schlund, wo viele ersticken. In dieser Nacht erreichen nur wenige die Feuerschalen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The smoke drives the crows into the Throat, where many choke. That night few of them reach the braziers."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El humo empuja a los cuervos hacia la Garganta, donde muchos se ahogan. Esa noche pocos llegan a los braseros."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La fumée chasse les corneilles dans la Gorge, où beaucoup s’étouffent. Cette nuit-là, peu d’entre elles atteignent les braseros."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il fumo spinge le cornacchie nella Gola, dove molte soffocano. Quella notte poche raggiungono i bracieri."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "煙が烏を喉谷へ追い込み、その多くがむせて落ちる。その夜、篝火までたどり着く烏はわずかだ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A fumaça empurra os corvos para a Garganta, onde muitos sufocam. Naquela noite, poucos chegam aos braseiros."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "浓烟把鸦群赶进了喉谷，许多被呛死了。那一夜，飞到火盆跟前的寥寥无几。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Am Abend hat jedes Feld eine Strohwache, jede wie jemand vom Hof gekleidet. Die von Odile ist die furchterregendste."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "By evening every field has a straw guard, each dressed like someone at court. Odile’s is the most frightening."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al anochecer cada campo tiene un guardián de paja, cada uno vestido como alguien de la corte. El de Odile es el que más miedo da."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le soir, chaque champ a son garde de paille, chacun habillé comme quelqu’un de la cour. Celui d’Odile est le plus effrayant."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Entro sera ogni campo ha una guardia di paglia, ognuna vestita come qualcuno della corte. Quella di Odile è la più spaventosa."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "夕方には、どの畑にも藁の番人が立つ。それぞれ城の誰かの格好をしている。オディールのがいちばん恐ろしい。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "À noitinha, cada campo tem um guarda de palha, cada um vestido como alguém da corte. O de Odile é o mais assustador."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "到傍晚，每块田都有了一个稻草守卫，个个扮成城堡里的某个人。奥黛尔那个最吓人。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Bauer starrt Euch lange an. Dann geht er heim und setzt sich auf sein Feld, nur um im Weg zu sein."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The farmer stares at you for a long time. Then he goes home and sits in his field, just to be in the way."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El campesino se le queda mirando largo rato. Luego se va a casa y se sienta en su campo, solo para estorbar."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le paysan vous fixe longuement. Puis il rentre et s’assied dans son champ, rien que pour gêner."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il contadino vi fissa a lungo. Poi torna a casa e si siede nel suo campo, solo per stare in mezzo ai piedi."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "農夫は長いあいだ、こちらを見つめる。それから家に帰り、邪魔をするためだけに、自分の畑に座り込む。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O camponês encara você por um longo tempo. Depois vai para casa e se senta no meio do campo, só para atrapalhar."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "农夫盯着你看了很久。然后他回了家，坐在自己的田里，就为了碍事。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_plague.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_plague (farmer, endless only): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, die Rußkrähen haben die Felder entdeckt. Sie fressen die Saat nicht. Sie sitzen darauf, zu Hunderten, und die Saat wird grau. Ich kann die Stoppeln abbrennen, um sie zu vertreiben, oder wir versuchen es mit Vogelscheuchen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, the soot crows have found the fields. They do not eat the seed. They sit on it, hundreds of them, and the seed turns grey. I can burn the stubble to drive them off, or we try scarecrows."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, los cuervos de hollín han encontrado los campos. No se comen la semilla. Se posan encima, cientos de ellos, y la semilla se vuelve gris. Puedo quemar el rastrojo para ahuyentarlos, o probamos con espantapájaros."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, les corneilles de suie ont trouvé les champs. Elles ne mangent pas les semences. Elles se posent dessus, par centaines, et les semences deviennent grises. Je peux brûler le chaume pour les chasser, ou on essaie les épouvantails."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, le cornacchie di fuliggine hanno trovato i campi. Non mangiano il seme. Ci si posano sopra, a centinaia, e il seme diventa grigio. Posso bruciare le stoppie per scacciarle, oppure proviamo con gli spaventapasseri."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、煤烏が畑を見つけました。種を食べるんじゃありません。何百羽も種の上に座り込んで、種が灰色になるんです。刈り株を焼いて追い払うこともできますし、案山子を試してみることも。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, os corvos de fuligem descobriram os campos. Não comem a semente. Sentam em cima dela, às centenas, e a semente fica cinzenta. Posso queimar o restolho para espantá-los, ou tentamos espantalhos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，煤鸦找到田里来了。它们不吃种子。它们成百上千地蹲在上面，种子就变灰了。我可以烧掉麦茬把它们赶走，要么我们试试稻草人。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_rags.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_rags: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bindet sie fest"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tie them on"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Átalos"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Noue-les"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Legali pure"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結んでおいで"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pode amarrar"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "去系吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_rags.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_rags: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Feuerschalen sind kein Spielzeug"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Braziers are no toys"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los braseros no son juguetes"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un brasero n’est pas un jouet"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I bracieri non sono giocattoli"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "篝火はおもちゃじゃないよ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Braseiro não é brinquedo"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "火盆不是玩具"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_rags.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_rags: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Kind hat öfter recht als die Generäle. Sagt ja."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The child is right more often than the generals. Say yes."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ese niño tiene razón más a menudo que los generales. Diga que sí."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant a raison plus souvent que les généraux. Dites oui."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino ha ragione più spesso dei generali. Dite di sì."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "あの子は、将軍たちより当たることが多いのです。はい、とお答えください。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A criança acerta mais vezes que os generais. Diga sim."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "这孩子说对的时候，比将军们还多。答应吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_rags.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_rags: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mit einem Arm voll rotem Stoff rennt das Kind davon. Heute Nacht ziehen die Krähen weite Kreise."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Off runs the child with an armful of red cloth. Tonight the crows circle wide."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Allá va el niño corriendo con una brazada de tela roja. Esta noche los cuervos vuelan en círculos bien abiertos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant détale, les bras chargés d’étoffe rouge. Cette nuit, les corneilles décrivent de larges cercles."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino corre via con una bracciata di stoffa rossa. Stanotte le cornacchie girano alla larga."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "赤い布を腕いっぱいに抱えて、子どもが駆けていく。今夜、烏たちは大きく弧を描き、遠巻きに飛ぶ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lá se vai a criança correndo, com uma braçada de pano vermelho. Esta noite, os corvos voam em círculos largos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子抱着一大把红布跑开了。今夜，鸦群绕得远远的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_rags.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_rags: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein Stampfen, und weg. Hinterher sind der Wache am Tor rätselhafterweise beide Stiefel aufgeschnürt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A stamped foot, and gone. The guard says his bootlaces came undone on the way out."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un pisotón, y se va. El guardia cuenta que, al salir, se le desataron los cordones de las botas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un coup de pied par terre, et l’enfant a filé. Le garde dit que ses lacets se sont dénoués au passage."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Batte i piedi, e sparisce. La guardia racconta che, al passaggio del bambino, gli si sono sciolti i lacci degli stivali."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "どんと足を踏み鳴らして、行ってしまう。衛兵が言うには、その子が出ていったあと、自分の長靴の紐がほどけていたという。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Um pé batido no chão, e sumiu. O guarda diz que, na saída, os cordões das botas dele se soltaram."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "跺一下脚，人就没影了。孩子走后，门口的卫兵发现自己的鞋带莫名其妙地散了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.crow_rags.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition crow_rags (child): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bitte, {Burgherr|Burgherrin}, Rußkrähen hassen bunte Lumpen! Meine Oma sagt das. Lasst mich vor der Dunkelheit rote Lumpen um die Feuerschalen binden, dann bleiben sie weg. Sechs habe ich schon gebunden."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Please, my {lord|lady}, soot crows hate bright rags! My gran says so. Let me tie red rags round the braziers before dark and they will keep away. I tied six already."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "¡Por favor, {mi señor|mi señora}, los cuervos de hollín odian los trapos de colores! Lo dice mi abuela. Déjeme atar trapos rojos a los braseros antes de que oscurezca y no se acercarán. Ya até seis."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "S’il vous plaît, {monseigneur|madame}, les corneilles de suie détestent les chiffons vifs ! C’est ma mémé qui le dit. Laissez-moi nouer des chiffons rouges autour des braseros avant la nuit, et elles resteront loin. J’en ai déjà noué six."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Per favore, {mio signore|mia signora}, le cornacchie di fuliggine odiano gli stracci colorati! Lo dice mia nonna. Lasciatemi legare stracci rossi intorno ai bracieri prima che faccia buio, e staranno lontane. Ne ho già legati sei."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "お願い、城主様、煤烏は派手なぼろ布が大嫌いなの！　おばあちゃんがそう言ってた。暗くなる前に、篝火に赤いぼろを結ばせて。そしたら近寄ってこないよ。もう六つ結んだの。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Por favor, {meu senhor|minha senhora}, corvo de fuligem odeia trapo colorido! Minha avó que falou. Me deixe amarrar trapos vermelhos nos braseiros antes de escurecer, e eles vão ficar longe. Já amarrei seis."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "求您了，城主大人，煤鸦最讨厌鲜艳的破布！我奶奶说的。让我天黑前在火盆上系红布条，它们就不敢过来了。我已经系了六个。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Auspeitschen, wie es das Gesetz will"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Flog him, as the law says"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Azotarlo, como manda la ley"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le fouet, comme le veut la loi"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Frustarlo, come vuole la legge"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "掟どおり、鞭打ちだ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Açoitar, como manda a lei"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "按律鞭打他"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Schickt ihn heim in die Stadt"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Send him home to the town"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que vuelva a casa, al pueblo"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Renvoyez-le chez lui, en ville"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rimandatelo a casa, nel borgo"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "町へ帰してやってくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mande-o de volta para a cidade"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "送他回镇上"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Begnadigt, zurück auf die Mauer"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pardon him, back to the wall"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Perdonado, y de vuelta a la muralla"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pardonné, retour sur la muraille"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Graziato. Torni sulle mura."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "赦す。城壁へ戻ってくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Perdoado, de volta à muralha"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "饶了他，回城墙去"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein ausgepeitschter Soldat bleibt ein Soldat, und die anderen werden sich an die Peitsche erinnern. Begnadigt ihn einmal."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A flogged soldier is still a soldier, and the others will remember the flogging. Pardon him once."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un soldado azotado sigue siendo un soldado, y los demás recordarán los azotes. Perdónelo una vez."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un soldat fouetté reste un soldat, et les autres se souviendront du fouet. Pardonnez-lui, une fois."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un soldato frustato resta un soldato, e gli altri si ricorderanno la frusta. Graziatelo, per questa volta."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "鞭打たれた兵も兵には変わりませんが、ほかの者は鞭のことを覚えています。一度だけ、お赦しなさいませ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Um soldado açoitado continua soldado, e os outros vão se lembrar do açoite. Perdoe-o uma vez."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "挨过鞭子的兵还是兵，可别人会记住那顿鞭子。饶他这一回。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Junge nimmt die Hiebe ohne einen Laut. In der Nacht steht er auf seinem Posten und weicht keinen Schritt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The boy takes his strokes without a sound. That night he stands his post and does not move a step."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El muchacho recibe los azotes sin un quejido. Esa noche se mantiene en su puesto y no retrocede ni un paso."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le garçon reçoit ses coups sans un bruit. Cette nuit-là, il tient son poste et ne recule pas d’un pas."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il ragazzo prende i colpi senza un lamento. Quella notte resta al suo posto e non arretra di un passo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "若者は声ひとつ立てずに鞭を受ける。その夜、持ち場に立ち、一歩も動かない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O rapaz recebe as chicotadas sem um som. Naquela noite, fica no seu posto e não recua um passo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "那小子挨鞭子时一声不吭。那一夜，他守在岗位上，寸步不移。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er gibt seinen Bogen ab und geht heim in die Backstube seiner Mutter. Brannock nennt es Verschwendung. Die Backstube nicht."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He hands in his bow and goes home to his mother’s bakery. Brannock calls it a waste. The bakery does not."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Entrega su arco y vuelve a la panadería de su madre. Brannock lo llama un desperdicio. La panadería, no."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il rend son arc et rentre à la boulangerie de sa mère. Brannock parle de gâchis. La boulangerie, non."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Consegna l’arco e torna a casa, nel forno di sua madre. Brannock lo chiama uno spreco. Il forno no."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "彼は弓を返し、母親のパン屋へ帰っていく。ブラノックはもったいないと言う。パン屋はそう言わない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele entrega o arco e volta para a padaria da mãe. Brannock chama isso de desperdício. A padaria, não."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他交了弓，回到母亲的面包坊。布兰诺克说这是浪费。面包坊可不这么想。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Junge weint, salutiert und weint wieder. Brannock sagt nichts, stellt ihn aber auf der Mauer neben sich."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The boy weeps, salutes, then weeps again. Brannock says nothing, but puts the lad next to himself on the wall."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El muchacho llora, saluda y vuelve a llorar. Brannock no dice nada, pero lo pone a su lado en la muralla."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le garçon pleure, salue, puis pleure encore. Brannock ne dit rien, mais place le gars à côté de lui sur la muraille."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il ragazzo piange, saluta, poi piange di nuovo. Brannock non dice niente, ma sulle mura lo mette accanto a sé."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "若者は泣き、敬礼し、また泣く。ブラノックは何も言わないが、城壁で彼を自分の隣に立たせる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O rapaz chora, bate continência e chora de novo. Brannock não diz nada, mas o coloca junto de si na muralha."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "那小子哭了，敬了个礼，又哭了。布兰诺克什么也没说，却把他安排在城墙上自己身边。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.deserter.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition deserter (soldier): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Herr|Herrin}, der Junge ist von der mittleren Linie gelaufen, als die Hunde kamen. Brannock will ihn auspeitschen lassen. Er ist der Sohn meiner Schwester. Er läuft nicht wieder weg. Das schwöre ich auf meinen eigenen Schild."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, the boy ran from the middle line when the hounds came. Brannock wants him flogged. He is my sister’s son. He will not run again. I swear it on my own shield."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Señor|Señora}, el muchacho huyó de la línea central cuando llegaron los sabuesos. Brannock quiere azotarlo. Es el hijo de mi hermana. No volverá a huir. Lo juro por mi propio escudo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, le garçon a fui la ligne du milieu quand les chiens sont venus. Brannock veut le faire fouetter. C’est le fils de ma sœur. Il ne fuira plus. Je le jure sur mon propre bouclier."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Signore|Signora}, il ragazzo è scappato dalla linea di mezzo quando sono arrivati i segugi. Brannock vuole farlo frustare. È il figlio di mia sorella. Non scapperà più. Lo giuro sul mio scudo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主。影犬が来たとき、あの小僧は中の防衛線から逃げました。ブラノック隊長は鞭打ちだと言っています。あれは私の姉の息子です。二度と逃げません。私自身の盾にかけて誓います。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Senhor|Senhora}, o rapaz fugiu da linha do meio quando os cães vieram. Brannock quer que ele seja açoitado. É filho da minha irmã. Não vai fugir de novo. Juro pelo meu próprio escudo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主，影犬来的时候，那小子从中防线跑了。布兰诺克要抽他鞭子。他是我外甥。他不会再跑了。我拿自己的盾牌起誓。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Entzündet die Feuerkörbe"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Light the fire-baskets"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Encienda los cestos de fuego"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Allumez les corbeilles à feu"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Accendete i cesti di fuoco"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "火籠をともしてください"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Acendam os cestos de fogo"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "点燃火篮吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Betet stattdessen mit mir"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pray with me instead"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mejor rece conmigo"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Priez plutôt avec moi"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pregate con me, piuttosto"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "代わりに、一緒に祈ってください"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Em vez disso, reze comigo"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "请您与我一同祈祷"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Omen sind etwas für Priester"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Omens are for priests"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los presagios son cosa de sacerdotes"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les présages, affaire de prêtres"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I presagi sono roba da preti"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兆しは司祭の領分です"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Presságio é coisa de sacerdote"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "预兆是祭司的事"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Öl ist billiger als Särge, und beim Mond irrt die Flamme selten. Entzündet die Feuerkörbe."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oil is cheaper than coffins, and the Flame is rarely wrong about the moon. Light the fire-baskets."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El aceite es más barato que los ataúdes, y la Llama rara vez se equivoca con la luna. Encienda los cestos de fuego."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’huile coûte moins cher que les cercueils, et la Flamme se trompe rarement sur la lune. Allumez les corbeilles à feu."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’olio costa meno delle bare, e sulla luna la Fiamma sbaglia di rado. Accendete i cesti di fuoco."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "油は棺より安く、月のことで炎が外れることは、めったにございません。火籠を灯すのが賢明かと。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Óleo é mais barato que caixões, e a Chama raramente erra sobre a lua. Acenda os cestos de fogo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "灯油比棺材便宜，而圣焰看月亮很少出错。点燃火篮。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Simse brennen die ganze Nacht wie eine Lichterkette. Der Mond wird schwarz, und der Schlund bleibt hell vom Rand bis zum Grund."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The ledges burn like a string of lamps all night. The moon goes black, and the Throat stays lit from rim to floor."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Las cornisas arden toda la noche como un collar de lámparas. La luna se vuelve negra, y la Garganta sigue iluminada del borde al fondo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les corniches brûlent toute la nuit comme un chapelet de lampes. La lune noircit, et la Gorge reste éclairée du rebord jusqu’au fond."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le cenge ardono tutta la notte come una fila di lampade. La luna diventa nera, e la Gola resta illuminata dall’orlo al fondo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "岩棚は夜通し、連なる灯火のように燃える。月は黒くなり、喉谷は縁から底まで明るいままだ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "As saliências ardem a noite inteira como um colar de lampiões. A lua fica negra, e a Garganta continua iluminada da borda ao fundo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "崖架彻夜燃烧，像一串灯火。月亮黑了，喉谷从崖顶到谷底依旧通明。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Kapelle füllt sich, und die Stadt betet mit Euch. Der Mond wird trotzdem schwarz, und die Düsternis kommt dicht."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The chapel fills, and the town prays with you. The moon goes black anyway, and the Gloom comes thick."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La capilla se llena, y el pueblo reza con usted. La luna se vuelve negra de todos modos, y la Penumbra llega espesa."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La chapelle se remplit, et la ville prie avec vous. La lune noircit quand même, et la Pénombre vient en masse."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La cappella si riempie, e il borgo prega con voi. La luna diventa nera lo stesso, e la Penombra arriva fitta."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "礼拝堂は人であふれ、町はともに祈る。それでも月は黒くなり、宵闇が濃く押し寄せる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A capela se enche, e a cidade reza com você. A lua fica negra mesmo assim, e a Penumbra vem espessa."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "礼拜堂里坐满了人，全镇与你一同祈祷。月亮还是黑了，暗霭来得又浓又密。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.r3a" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: choice 3, it went well.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Mond bleibt die ganze Nacht silbern. Hesper sagt beim Frühstück nichts, und zwar sehr laut."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The moon stays silver all night. Hesper says nothing at breakfast, very loudly."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La luna sigue plateada toda la noche. En el desayuno, Hesper guarda un silencio atronador."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La lune reste d’argent toute la nuit. Au matin, à table, Hesper ne dit rien, très fort."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La luna resta d’argento per tutta la notte. A colazione Hesper osserva un silenzio assordante."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "月は夜通し銀色のままだ。朝食の席で、ヘスパーは何も言わない。とても大きな声で。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A lua fica prateada a noite toda. No café da manhã, Hesper não diz nada, em alto e bom som."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "月亮整夜都是银色的。早饭时赫斯珀一言不发，沉默得震耳欲聋。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.r3b" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen: choice 3, it went badly.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Um Mitternacht erlischt der Mond wie ein zugedrückter Docht, und die Düsternis kommt in doppelten Reihen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "At midnight the moon goes out like a pinched wick, and the Gloom comes in doubled ranks."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A medianoche la luna se apaga como una mecha pellizcada, y la Penumbra viene en filas dobles."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "À minuit, la lune s’éteint comme une mèche pincée, et la Pénombre vient en rangs doublés."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A mezzanotte la luna si spegne come uno stoppino pizzicato, e la Penombra arriva a ranghi doppi."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "真夜中、つまんで消した灯心のように月が消え、宵闇が倍の列を組んで来る。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "À meia-noite, a lua se apaga como um pavio apertado entre os dedos, e a Penumbra vem em fileiras dobradas."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "半夜，月亮像被掐灭的灯芯一样熄了，暗霭的阵列厚了一倍，涌了上来。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.eclipse_omen.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition eclipse_omen (hesper, endless only): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Erbe|Erbin} des Hauses, die Flamme sagt, heute Nacht wird der Mond schwarz. In solchen Nächten kommt die Düsternis in doppelten Reihen. Die alten Feuerkörbe auf den Simsen des Schlunds könnten das Dunkel zurückhalten, wenn jemand das Öl bezahlt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Heir of the house, the Flame says the moon goes black tonight. On such nights the Gloom comes in doubled ranks. The old fire-baskets on the Throat’s ledges could hold the dark back, if someone pays for the oil."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Hijo|Hija} de la casa, la Llama dice que esta noche la luna se volverá negra. En noches así, la Penumbra viene en filas dobles. Los viejos cestos de fuego de las cornisas de la Garganta podrían contener la oscuridad, si alguien paga el aceite."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Enfant de la maison, la Flamme dit que la lune va noircir cette nuit. Ces nuits-là, la Pénombre vient en rangs doublés. Les vieilles corbeilles à feu sur les corniches de la Gorge pourraient tenir l’obscurité en respect, si quelqu’un paie l’huile."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Figlio|Figlia} della casa, la Fiamma dice che stanotte la luna diventerà nera. In notti così la Penombra arriva a ranghi doppi. I vecchi cesti di fuoco sulle cenge della Gola potrebbero tenere indietro il buio, se qualcuno paga l’olio."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "家の御子、今夜は月が黒くなると、炎が告げています。そういう夜には、宵闇が倍の列を組んで来るのです。喉谷の岩棚にある古い火籠なら、闇を押しとどめられるでしょう。誰かが油代を払えば。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Filho|Filha} da casa, a Chama diz que a lua fica negra esta noite. Em noites assim, a Penumbra vem em fileiras dobradas. Os velhos cestos de fogo nas saliências da Garganta poderiam conter o escuro, se alguém pagar o óleo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "家族之子，圣焰说今夜月亮要变黑。这样的夜里，暗霭的阵列会厚上一倍。喉谷崖架上的旧火篮能挡住黑暗，只要有人出灯油钱。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_coast.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_coast: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Schickt zwei Schützen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Send two archers"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que vayan dos arqueros"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Envoyez deux archers"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mandate due arcieri"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
