          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_coast.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_coast: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Silber für zwei Schützen, während die Düsternis jede Nacht kommt. Die Küste kann für uns beten. Lehnt ab, höflich."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Silver for two archers, while the Gloom comes nightly. The coast can pray for us. Refuse, politely."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Plata por dos arqueros, mientras la Penumbra viene cada noche. Que la costa rece por nosotros. Niéguese, con cortesía."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "De l’argent pour deux archers, alors que la Pénombre vient chaque nuit. La côte peut prier pour nous. Refusez, poliment."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Argento per due arcieri, mentre la Penombra viene ogni notte. La costa può pregare per noi. Rifiutate, con garbo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "宵闇が毎晩来るというのに、弓兵2人に銀貨とは。沿岸には、我らのために祈っていただきましょう。お断りください。丁重に。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Prata por dois arqueiros, enquanto a Penumbra vem toda noite. A costa pode rezar por nós. Recuse, com educação."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "拿银子换两名弓手，而暗霭夜夜都来。海岸可以为我们祈祷。拒绝，客气些。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_coast.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_coast: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zwei Freiwillige reiten im Morgengrauen mit dem Gesandten zur Küste. Odile zählt das Silber zweimal und nennt es Diplomatie."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Two volunteers ride for the coast with the envoy at dawn. Odile counts the silver twice and calls it diplomacy."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dos voluntarios parten al alba hacia la costa con el enviado. Odile cuenta la plata dos veces y lo llama diplomacia."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "À l’aube, deux volontaires partent pour la côte avec l’envoyé. Odile compte l’argent deux fois et appelle cela de la diplomatie."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "All’alba due volontari partono a cavallo per la costa con l’inviato. Odile conta l’argento due volte e la chiama diplomazia."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "夜明け、志願した二人が使節とともに沿岸へ馬を走らせる。オディールは銀貨を二度数え、これを外交と呼ぶ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dois voluntários partem a cavalo para a costa com o enviado, na alvorada. Odile conta a prata duas vezes e chama isso de diplomacia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "黎明时，两名志愿者随使节骑马前往海岸。奥黛尔把银币数了两遍，管这叫外交。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_coast.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_coast: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Gesandte verneigt sich, nicht überrascht. „Dann betet, dass das Meer Eure Tür nie findet, {Lord|Lady} Lantern.“ Zurück bleibt ein Geruch nach Salz."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The envoy bows, unsurprised. “Then pray the sea never finds your door, {Lord|Lady} Lantern.” He leaves a smell of salt behind."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El enviado se inclina, sin sorpresa. «Entonces rece para que el mar nunca encuentre su puerta, {lord|lady} Lantern.» Deja tras de sí un olor a sal."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’envoyé s’incline, sans surprise. « Alors priez pour que la mer ne trouve jamais votre porte, {seigneur|dame} Lantern. » Il laisse derrière lui une odeur de sel."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’inviato si inchina, senza sorpresa. «Allora pregate che il mare non trovi mai la vostra porta, {Lord|Lady} Lantern.» Si lascia dietro un odore di sale."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "使節は驚きもせずに一礼する。「では、海がこちらの扉を見つけぬよう、お祈りなさいませ、ランタン様」。あとには潮の匂いが残る。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O enviado se curva, sem surpresa. “Então reze para que o mar nunca encontre a sua porta, {Lorde|Lady} Lantern.” Deixa para trás um cheiro de sal."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "使节躬身，并不意外。“那就祈祷大海永远找不到您的门吧，兰腾大人。”他身后留下一股咸味。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_coast.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_coast: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Gesandte nimmt das Öl mit echter Dankbarkeit an. „Die Küste wird sich an {Lord|Lady} Lantern erinnern“, sagt er, und er meint es."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The envoy accepts the oil with real gratitude. “The coast will remember {Lord|Lady} Lantern,” he says, and means it."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El enviado acepta el aceite con verdadera gratitud. «La costa recordará {al farolero|a la farolera}», dice, y lo dice en serio."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’envoyé accepte l’huile avec une vraie gratitude. « La côte se souviendra {du|de la} lampiste », dit-il, et il le pense."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’inviato accetta l’olio con sincera gratitudine. «La costa si ricorderà {del lampionaio|della lampionaia}», dice, e lo pensa davvero."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "使節は心から感謝して油を受け取る。「沿岸は、灯り番のことを忘れません」と言う。本心からだ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O enviado aceita o óleo com gratidão sincera. “A costa vai se lembrar {do acendedor de lampiões|da acendedora de lampiões}”, diz ele, e fala sério."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "使节真心感激地收下了灯油。“海岸会记住这位点灯人。”他说，这话出自真心。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_coast.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_coast (envoy): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, ich bringe schlechte Nachrichten von der Küste. Das Meer steigt jede Nacht höher, und Dinge klettern unsere Klippen hinauf, dem Leuchtturm entgegen. Meine Herrin bittet um zwei Schützen, die das Dunkel kennen. Sie zahlt in Silber."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, I bring ill news from the coast. The sea rises higher every night, and things climb our cliffs toward the lighthouse. My lady asks for two archers who know the dark. She repays in silver."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, traigo malas noticias de la costa. El mar sube más cada noche, y hay cosas que trepan por nuestros acantilados hacia el faro. Mi señora pide dos arqueros que conozcan la oscuridad. Paga en plata."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Seigneur|Dame} Lantern, j’apporte de mauvaises nouvelles de la côte. La mer monte plus haut chaque nuit, et des choses escaladent nos falaises vers le phare. Madame demande deux archers qui connaissent l’obscurité. Elle paiera en pièces d’argent."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, porto cattive notizie dalla costa. Il mare sale ogni notte di più, e delle cose si arrampicano sulle nostre scogliere verso il faro. La mia signora chiede due arcieri che conoscano il buio. Ripagherà in argento."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ランタン様、沿岸から悪い知らせを持ってまいりました。海は夜ごとに高くなり、何かが崖をよじ登って灯台へ向かってきます。我が主は、闇を知る弓兵を2人お貸しいただきたいと。お礼は銀貨でお支払いします。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lorde|Lady} Lantern, trago más notícias da costa. O mar sobe mais a cada noite, e coisas escalam os nossos penhascos rumo ao nosso farol. A minha senhora pede dois arqueiros que conheçam o escuro. Ela paga em prata."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兰腾大人，我从海岸带来坏消息。海水一夜比一夜涨得高，有东西顺着我们的悬崖往灯塔上爬。我家主人请求借两名识得黑暗的弓手。她会以银币相报。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_tide.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_tide: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Tor wird sich öffnen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The gate will open"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La puerta se abrirá"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La porte s’ouvrira"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La porta si aprirà"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "門は開く"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O portão vai se abrir"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城门会打开"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_tide.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_tide: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das können wir nicht versprechen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "We cannot promise that"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eso no podemos prometerlo"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nous ne pouvons pas promettre cela"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Non possiamo promettervelo"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "それは約束できない"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Não podemos prometer isso"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "这个我们不能承诺"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_tide.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_tide: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein Versprechen für eine Truhe Fisch. Diesen Handel würde ich jeden Tag machen. Versprecht es."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A promise for a chest of fish. I would make that trade every day of the week. Promise."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una promesa por un arcón de pescado. Haría ese trato todos los días de la semana. Prométalo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Une promesse contre un coffre de poisson. Je ferais ce marché tous les jours de la semaine. Promettez."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una promessa in cambio di una cassa di pesce. Farei questo scambio tutti i giorni della settimana. Promettete."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "魚ひと箱で約束ひとつ。毎日でもしたい取引です。迷うまでもございません。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Uma promessa por um baú de peixe. Eu faria essa troca todos os dias da semana. Prometa."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一个承诺换一箱鱼。这样的买卖我天天都做。答应她。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_tide.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_tide: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Gesandte kniet nieder, was Gesandte nie tun. Später verkauft Odile den Salzfisch auf dem Markt und summt dabei."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The envoy kneels, which envoys never do. Later Odile sells the salt fish at the market, humming."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El enviado se arrodilla, cosa que los enviados nunca hacen. Más tarde, Odile vende el pescado en el mercado, tarareando."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’envoyé s’agenouille, ce que les envoyés ne font jamais. Plus tard, Odile vend le poisson salé au marché en fredonnant."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’inviato si inginocchia, cosa che gli inviati non fanno mai. Più tardi Odile vende il pesce salato al mercato, canticchiando."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "使節がひざまずく。使節というものが、決してしないことだ。のちにオディールは、鼻歌まじりに塩漬けの魚を市場で売りさばく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O enviado se ajoelha, coisa que enviados nunca fazem. Mais tarde, Odile vende o peixe salgado no mercado, cantarolando."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "使节跪了下来，而使节是从不下跪的。后来奥黛尔哼着歌，把咸鱼拿到集市上卖了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_tide.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_tide: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er lässt den Fisch trotzdem da. „Für Eure Schützen“, sagt er. „Irgendwer sollte vor dem Ende gut essen.“"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He leaves the fish anyway. “For your archers,” he says. “Someone should eat well before the end.”"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Deja el pescado de todos modos. «Para sus arqueros», dice. «Alguien debería comer bien antes del final.»"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il laisse le poisson quand même. « Pour vos archers, dit-il. Quelqu’un devrait bien manger avant la fin. »"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lascia il pesce lo stesso. «Per i vostri arcieri», dice. «Qualcuno dovrebbe mangiare bene, prima della fine.»"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "それでも彼は魚を置いていく。「弓兵の方々に」と言う。「終わりの前に、誰かがうまいものを食べるべきです」"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele deixa o peixe mesmo assim. “Para os seus arqueiros”, diz ele. “Alguém deveria comer bem antes do fim.”"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他还是把鱼留下了。“给您的弓手，”他说，“总该有人在终局前吃顿好的。”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.envoy_tide.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition envoy_tide (envoy): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, noch einmal die Küste. Die schwarze Flut hat unseren unteren Hafen geholt. Meine Herrin schickt eine Truhe Salzfisch und bittet um eines: Wenn die Küste fällt, öffnet sich dann Euer Tor für ihre Leute?"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, the coast again. The black tide took our lower harbour. My lady sends a chest of salt fish and asks one thing: if the coast falls, will your gate open to its people?"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, otra vez la costa. La marejada negra se llevó nuestro puerto bajo. Mi señora envía un arcón de pescado en salazón y pide una sola cosa: si la costa cae, ¿abrirá usted su puerta a nuestra gente?"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Seigneur|Dame} Lantern, la côte, encore. Le flot noir a emporté notre port d’en bas. Madame envoie un coffre de poisson salé et demande une chose : si la côte tombe, votre porte s’ouvrira-t-elle à ses gens ?"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lord|Lady} Lantern, di nuovo la costa. La marea scura si è presa il nostro porto basso. La mia signora manda una cassa di pesce salato e chiede una cosa sola: se la costa cade, la vostra porta si aprirà alla sua gente?"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ランタン様、また沿岸の件です。黒い潮に、下の港を呑まれました。我が主は塩漬けの魚をひと箱お送りし、ひとつだけお尋ねします。沿岸が落ちたとき、こちらの門は、その民のために開くでしょうか。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Lorde|Lady} Lantern, a costa outra vez. A maré negra levou o nosso porto de baixo. A minha senhora envia um baú de peixe salgado e pede uma coisa: se a costa cair, o seu portão se abrirá para o povo dela?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兰腾大人，又是海岸。黑潮吞没了我们的下港。我家主人送来一箱咸鱼，只求一件事：倘若海岸失守，您的城门会为她的子民打开吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Geht mit meinem Segen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Go with my blessing"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vayan con mi bendición"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Allez avec ma bénédiction"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Andate con la mia benedizione"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "祝福を。道中、達者で"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vá com a minha bênção"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "带着我的祝福走吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bleibt, dieses Jahr zahlt das Haus"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Stay, and this year is on the house"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quédense: este año invita la casa"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Restez : cette année, c’est la maison qui paie"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Restate, e quest’anno paga la casata"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "残ってくれ。今年の分はお城が持つ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fique, e este ano a casa paga"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "留下吧，今年的税我来出"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Niemand verlässt das Tal"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nobody leaves the valley"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nadie deja el valle"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Personne ne quitte la vallée"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nessuno lascia la valle"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "谷を出ることは許さない"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ninguém deixa o vale"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "谁也不许离开河谷"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Drei Steuerzahler, die gehen, sind drei Steuerzahler, die gehen. Zwanzig Gold, um sie zu halten, sind ein Schnäppchen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Three taxpayers walking away is three taxpayers walking away. Twenty gold to keep them is a bargain."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tres contribuyentes que se van son tres contribuyentes que se van. Veinte monedas de oro por retenerlos son una ganga."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Trois contribuables qui s’en vont, ce sont trois contribuables qui s’en vont. Vingt pièces d’or pour les garder, c’est une affaire."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tre contribuenti che se ne vanno sono tre contribuenti che se ne vanno. Venti monete d’oro per tenerli sono un affare."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "納税者が3人出ていくのは、納税者が3人出ていくということです。引き止めるのに金貨20枚なら、安いものです。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Três contribuintes indo embora são três contribuintes indo embora. Vinte moedas de ouro para segurá-los é uma pechincha."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "三个纳税人走了，就是三个纳税人走了。花20金币留住他们，划算。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sie ziehen im Morgengrauen los, mit Handkarren und Ziege. Ihr Fenster bleibt dunkel, und die Gasse ist stiller, als sie sein sollte."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "They leave at dawn with a handcart and a goat. Their window stays dark, and the lane is quieter than it should be."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se marchan al alba con una carretilla y una cabra. Su ventana queda a oscuras, y la calle está más callada de lo que debería."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ils partent à l’aube avec une charrette à bras et une chèvre. Leur fenêtre reste éteinte, et la ruelle est plus calme qu’elle ne devrait."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Partono all’alba con un carretto a mano e una capra. La loro finestra resta buia, e il vicolo è più silenzioso di quanto dovrebbe."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一家は夜明けに、手押し車と山羊を連れて発つ。その窓は暗いままで、路地はあるべき姿より静かだ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Partem na alvorada com um carrinho de mão e uma cabra. A janela deles fica escura, e a viela fica mais quieta do que devia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他们黎明时推着一辆手推车、牵着一头山羊走了。他们的窗户一直黑着，巷子安静得不该如此。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er zögert, dann schlägt er ein. Am Abend schickt seine Frau eine Pastete hinauf, leicht verbrannt, als Friedensangebot."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He hesitates, then shakes your hand. That evening his wife sends up a pie, slightly burnt, as a peace offering."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Duda, y luego le estrecha la mano. Esa tarde su mujer le manda una empanada, algo quemada, en son de paz."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il hésite, puis vous serre la main. Le soir, sa femme fait monter une tourte, un peu brûlée, en gage de paix."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Esita, poi vi stringe la mano. Quella sera sua moglie manda su un pasticcio, un po’ bruciato, in segno di pace."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "男はためらい、それから手を握り返す。その晩、女房から、少し焦げたパイが仲直りのしるしに届く。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele hesita, depois aperta a sua mão. À noitinha, a mulher dele manda uma torta, um pouco queimada, como oferta de paz."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他犹豫了一下，然后握了握你的手。那天傍晚，他妻子送来一个馅饼，有点烤糊了，算是和解的礼物。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sie bleiben. Sie lächeln nicht. Am Abend lächelt auch sonst niemand in ihrer Gasse."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "They stay. They do not smile. Neither, by evening, does anyone else in their lane."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se quedan. No sonríen. Y al anochecer, nadie más en su calle sonríe tampoco."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ils restent. Ils ne sourient pas. Le soir venu, personne d’autre dans leur ruelle ne sourit non plus."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Restano. Non sorridono. Entro sera, non sorride più nessuno nel loro vicolo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一家は残る。笑顔はない。夕方には、その路地の誰からも笑顔が消えている。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eles ficam. Não sorriem. À noitinha, ninguém mais na viela deles sorri."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他们留下了。他们不笑。到傍晚，那条巷子里谁也不笑了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.family_leaving.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition family_leaving (townsman): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, meine Familie zieht an die Küste. Die Nächte sind zu laut, die Steuern zu hoch, und meine Frau sagt, ein Haus, das nie schläft, bleibt nicht stehen. Ich wollte es Euch nur ins Gesicht sagen, wie es sich gehört."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, my family is leaving for the coast. The nights are too loud, the taxes too high, and my wife says a house that never sleeps cannot stand. I only came to say it to your face, as is proper."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, mi familia se marcha a la costa. Las noches son demasiado ruidosas, los impuestos demasiado altos, y mi mujer dice que una casa que nunca duerme no puede tenerse en pie. Solo vine a decírselo a la cara, como es debido."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, ma famille part pour la côte. Les nuits sont trop bruyantes, les impôts trop lourds, et ma femme dit qu’une maison qui ne dort jamais ne peut pas tenir. Je suis seulement venu vous le dire en face, comme il se doit."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, la mia famiglia parte per la costa. Le notti sono troppo rumorose, le tasse troppo alte, e mia moglie dice che una casa che non dorme mai non può reggersi. Sono venuto solo a dirvelo in faccia, come si conviene."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、うちの家族は沿岸へ移ります。夜はうるさすぎるし、税は高すぎるし、女房は、眠らない家は立っていられないと言います。礼儀として、面と向かってお伝えしに来ただけです。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, a minha família vai embora para a costa. As noites são barulhentas demais, os impostos altos demais, e a minha mulher diz que uma casa que nunca dorme não fica de pé. Só vim dizer isso olhando nos seus olhos, como se deve."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我们一家要搬去海岸了。夜里太吵，税太重，我家那口子说，一个从不睡觉的家撑不久。我只是来当面说一声，这是规矩。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rückt ihn zurück"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Move it back"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pónganla en su sitio"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Remettez-la en place"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rimettetelo a posto"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "柵を戻してくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ponham de volta"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "挪回去"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Teilt den Fuß"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Split the foot"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Repartan el pie"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Coupez le pied en deux"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dividete il piede"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "足ひとつ分を半分ずつに"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dividam o palmo"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "那一尺对半分"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein Kohlrennen soll entscheiden"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Settle it with a cabbage race"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que lo decida una carrera de coles"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Une course de choux tranchera"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lo decida una gara di cavoli"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "キャベツ競争で決めよう"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Uma corrida de repolhos decide"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "用一场白菜赛跑来定"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rückt ihn zurück. Ein Zaun, der einmal geht, geht wieder, und bald wandert das ganze Tal."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Move it back. A fence that walks once will walk again, and soon the whole valley is moving."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Devuélvala a su sitio. Una cerca que anda una vez volverá a andar, y pronto se mudará el valle entero."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Remettez-la en place. Une clôture qui marche une fois marchera encore, et bientôt toute la vallée se promènera."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rimettetelo a posto. Uno steccato che cammina una volta camminerà ancora, e presto si sposterà tutta la valle."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "戻させなさいませ。一度歩いた柵はまた歩き、じきに谷じゅうが動き出します。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ponha de volta. Uma cerca que anda uma vez anda de novo, e logo o vale inteiro sai andando."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "挪回去。篱笆走过一回，就会再走，过不了多久，整个河谷都要搬家了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Zaun kommt zurück. Der Nachbar murmelt, er werde einfach wieder gehen. In dieser Nacht tut er es nicht, vielleicht aus Scham."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The fence goes back. The neighbour mutters that it will only walk again. That night it does not, possibly from shame."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La cerca vuelve a su sitio. El vecino masculla que volverá a andar. Esa noche no lo hace, quizá por vergüenza."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La clôture reprend sa place. Le voisin marmonne qu’elle remarchera. Cette nuit-là, elle ne bouge pas, peut-être par honte."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lo steccato torna indietro. Il vicino borbotta che tanto camminerà di nuovo. Quella notte non lo fa, forse per la vergogna."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "柵は元に戻る。隣の男は、どうせまた歩くさ、とつぶやく。その夜、柵は歩かない。恥じ入ったのかもしれない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A cerca volta para o lugar. O vizinho resmunga que ela só vai andar de novo. Naquela noite, ela não anda, talvez de vergonha."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "篱笆挪回去了。邻居嘟囔说它还会再走。那一夜它没走，也许是羞的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jeder bekommt einen halben Fuß. Beide murren. Daran erkennt man, dass es gerecht war."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Each gets half a foot. Both grumble. That is how you know it was fair."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada uno se queda con medio pie. Los dos refunfuñan. Así se sabe que fue justo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chacun reçoit un demi-pied. Les deux grognent. C’est à ça qu’on sait que c’était juste."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ciascuno ha mezzo piede. Tutti e due brontolano. È così che si capisce che è stato giusto."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "二人とも足半分ずつ得る。二人ともぼやく。それが公平だったという証だ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada um fica com meio palmo. Os dois resmungam. É assim que se sabe que foi justo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一人得了半尺。两人都嘟囔。这就说明分得公道。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.r3a" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: choice 3, it went well.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das ganze Tal kommt zum Zuschauen. Der Bittsteller gewinnt um einen Kohlkopf und wird im Triumph heimgetragen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The whole valley turns out to watch. The petitioner wins by a cabbage and is carried home in triumph."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Todo el valle sale a mirar. El peticionario gana por una col y lo llevan a casa en triunfo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Toute la vallée vient regarder. Le requérant gagne d’un chou et on le ramène chez lui en triomphe."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tutta la valle accorre a guardare. Il supplicante vince per un cavolo e viene riportato a casa in trionfo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "谷じゅうが見物に出てくる。訴えた男がキャベツ一個の差で勝ち、意気揚々と担がれて帰る。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O vale inteiro vem assistir. O peticionário vence por um repolho e é levado para casa em triunfo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "整个河谷都跑来看热闹。请愿人以一颗白菜之差获胜，被众人抬着凯旋回家。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.r3b" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud: choice 3, it went badly.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Nachbar gewinnt und behält den Fuß. Der Bittsteller schwört, die Kohlköpfe seien verhext gewesen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The neighbour wins and keeps the foot. The petitioner swears the cabbages were enchanted."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gana el vecino y se queda el pie. El peticionario jura que las coles estaban embrujadas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le voisin gagne et garde le pied. Le requérant jure que les choux étaient ensorcelés."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vince il vicino, che si tiene il piede. Il supplicante giura che i cavoli erano stregati."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "隣の男が勝ち、足ひとつ分を手に入れる。訴えた男は、キャベツに魔法がかけられていたと言い張る。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O vizinho vence e fica com o palmo. O peticionário jura que os repolhos estavam enfeitiçados."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "邻居赢了，留下了那一尺。请愿人发誓说那些白菜被施了法。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.fence_feud.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition fence_feud (farmer, endless only): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, mein Nachbar hat unseren Zaun in der Nacht einen Fuß weit auf mein Land gerückt. Er sagt, der Zaun sei von selbst gegangen, aus Angst vor der Düsternis. Zäune gehen nicht. Ich will meinen Fuß zurück."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, my neighbour moved our fence a foot onto my land in the night. He says the fence walked by itself, out of fear of the Gloom. Fences do not walk. I want my foot back."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, mi vecino movió de noche nuestra cerca un pie dentro de mi tierra. Dice que la cerca echó a andar sola, del miedo a la Penumbra. Las cercas no andan. Quiero que me devuelvan mi pie."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, mon voisin a déplacé notre clôture d’un pied sur ma terre pendant la nuit. Il dit que la clôture a marché toute seule, par peur de la Pénombre. Les clôtures ne marchent pas. Je veux qu’on me rende mon pied."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, di notte il mio vicino ha spostato il nostro steccato di un piede dentro la mia terra. Dice che lo steccato ha camminato da solo, per paura della Penombra. Gli steccati non camminano. Rivoglio il mio piede."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、隣の男が夜のうちに、境の柵を足ひとつ分、うちの土地に動かしたんです。宵闇が怖くて柵がひとりでに歩いた、なんて言います。柵は歩きません。私の足を返してほしい。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, o meu vizinho mudou a nossa cerca um palmo para dentro da minha terra durante a noite. Diz que a cerca andou sozinha, com medo da Penumbra. Cerca não anda. Quero o meu palmo de volta."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我邻居半夜把我们之间的篱笆往我地里挪了一尺。他说篱笆是自己走的，因为怕暗霭。篱笆不会走路。我要把我那一尺要回来。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.first_plough.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition first_plough: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Den Pflug segnen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bless the plough"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bendecir el arado"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bénir la charrue"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Benedire l’aratro"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "鋤を祝福する"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Abençoar o arado"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "为犁祝福"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.first_plough.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition first_plough: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Ein Burgherr|Eine Burgherrin} segnet keine Werkzeuge"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A {lord|lady} blesses no tools"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Un señor|Una señora} no bendice herramientas"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Un seigneur|Une dame} ne bénit pas d’outils"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Un signore|Una signora} non benedice attrezzi"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主は道具を祝福しない"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Um senhor|Uma senhora} não abençoa ferramentas"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主不为农具祝福"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.first_plough.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition first_plough: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jede Antwort kostet Gold oder Wohlwollen, {Burgherr|Burgherrin} {lord}. Diese kostet einen Segen, und Segen sind umsonst. Segnet den Pflug."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Every answer costs gold or goodwill, {Lord|Lady} {lord}. This one costs a blessing, and blessings are free. Bless the plough."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada respuesta cuesta oro o buena voluntad, {lord|lady} {lord}. Esta cuesta una bendición, y las bendiciones son gratis. Bendiga el arado."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chaque réponse coûte de l’or ou de la bonne volonté, {Seigneur|Dame} {lord}. Celle-ci coûte une bénédiction, et les bénédictions sont gratuites. Bénissez la charrue."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ogni risposta costa oro o benevolenza, {Lord|Lady} {lord}. Questa costa una benedizione, e le benedizioni sono gratis. Benedite l’aratro."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "どの答えにも、金か好意かの代償がございます、{lord}様。この件の代償は祝福ひとつ。祝福はただです。鋤に祝福を。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Toda resposta custa ouro ou boa vontade, {Lorde|Lady} {lord}. Esta custa uma bênção, e bênçãos são de graça. Abençoe o arado."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "每个答复都要花金子或人心，{lord}大人。这一个只花一句祝福，而祝福不要钱。为犁祝福吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.first_plough.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition first_plough: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er strahlt, küsst die Pflugschar und läuft los, um es bis Mittag dem halben Tal zu erzählen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He beams, kisses the blade and runs off to tell half the valley before noon."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se le ilumina la cara, besa la reja y sale corriendo a contárselo a medio valle antes del mediodía."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il rayonne, embrasse le soc et file le raconter à la moitié de la vallée avant midi."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Si illumina, bacia il vomere e corre via a raccontarlo a mezza valle prima di mezzogiorno."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "農夫は顔をほころばせ、刃に口づけし、昼までに谷の半分に触れ回ろうと駆け出していく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele abre um sorriso, beija a lâmina e sai correndo para contar a meio vale antes do meio-dia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他满脸放光，亲了亲犁铧，一溜烟跑了，不到中午就告诉了半个河谷。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.first_plough.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition first_plough: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er schlurft hinaus. Ihr hört ihn der Wache sagen, Aldric habe alles gesegnet, sogar Ziegen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He shuffles out. You hear him tell the guard that Lord Aldric blessed everything, even goats."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sale arrastrando los pies. Lo oye decirle al guardia que, total, el aro le viene grande."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il sort en traînant les pieds. Vous l’entendez dire au garde que le cercle est bien trop grand, de toute façon."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Esce strascicando i piedi. Lo sentite dire alla guardia che tanto il cerchio è troppo grande."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "農夫はとぼとぼと出ていく。どうせ額輪が大きすぎるのさ、と衛兵にこぼすのが聞こえる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele sai arrastando os pés. Você o ouve dizer ao guarda que, de todo modo, o aro parece grande demais."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他拖着脚走了出去。你听见他对卫兵说，反正那额环看着也太大了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.first_plough.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition first_plough (farmer, story day 1): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}! Der Frost hat mir den Pflug gesprengt, just an dem Morgen, als der Stirnreif an Euch ging. Die Leute sagen, die Hand {eines neuen Burgherrn|einer neuen Burgherrin} bringt Glück. Segnet Ihr den neuen, bevor ich das lange Feld umbreche?"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}! The frost cracked my plough on the very morning the circlet passed. Folk say a new {lord|lady}’s touch brings luck. Would you bless the new one before I break the long field?"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "¡{Mi señor|Mi señora}! La helada me partió el arado justo la mañana en que el aro cambió de dueño. Dicen que la mano de {un señor nuevo|una señora nueva} trae suerte. ¿Me bendice el nuevo antes de arar el campo largo?"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame} ! Le gel a fendu ma charrue le matin même où le cercle a changé de tête. On dit que la main {d’un nouveau seigneur|d’une nouvelle dame} porte bonheur. Voulez-vous bénir la neuve avant que j’entame le long champ ?"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}! Il gelo mi ha spaccato l’aratro proprio la mattina in cui il cerchio è passato a voi. La gente dice che la mano di {un nuovo signore|una nuova signora} porta fortuna. Benedireste quello nuovo, prima che dissodi il campo lungo?"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様！　額輪が渡ったまさにその朝、霜で鋤が割れてしまいました。新しい城主様に触れていただくと運が向く、と皆が申します。長い畑を起こす前に、新しい鋤を祝福していただけませんか。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}! A geada rachou o meu arado justo na manhã em que o aro trocou de dono. O povo diz que a mão de {um senhor novo|uma senhora nova} dá sorte. Poderia abençoar o arado novo antes que eu lavre o campo grande?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人！额环传到您手上的那天早上，霜把我的犁冻裂了。人们都说，新城主摸一摸能带来好运。在我翻那块长田之前，您能给新犁祝个福吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.footbridge.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition footbridge: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
