            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "人人可以自己定价"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.miller_hoard.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition miller_hoard: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zwingt einen Müller, und jeder Händler im Tal versteckt seine Ware. Lasst den Markt das regeln."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Force one miller and every merchant in the valley hides his goods. Let the market sort him out."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Obligue a un molinero, y todos los mercaderes del valle esconderán sus géneros. Deje que el mercado lo ponga en su sitio."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Forcez un meunier, et tous les marchands de la vallée cacheront leurs marchandises. Laissez le marché le remettre à sa place."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Obbligate un mugnaio, e ogni mercante della valle nasconderà la merce. Lasciate che ci pensi il mercato."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "粉屋ひとりを無理に従わせれば、谷じゅうの商人が品を隠します。始末は市場に任せるのが一番です。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Force um moleiro, e todo mercador do vale esconde a mercadoria. Deixe o mercado dar um jeito nele."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "逼一个磨坊主开门，河谷里每个商人都会把货藏起来。让市面去收拾他。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.miller_hoard.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition miller_hoard: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mittags brechen die Wachen das Schloss auf. Die Mütter jubeln, und der Müller schreibt einen langen Brief an einen sehr wichtigen Herrn."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The guards break the lock at noon. The mothers cheer, and the miller writes a long letter to somebody important."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los guardias rompen el candado al mediodía. Las madres aplauden, y el molinero escribe una larga carta a alguien importante."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les gardes forcent la serrure à midi. Les mères applaudissent, et le meunier écrit une longue lettre à quelqu’un d’important."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A mezzogiorno le guardie forzano il lucchetto. Le madri esultano, e il mugnaio scrive una lunga lettera a qualcuno di importante."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "昼、衛兵が錠を壊す。母親たちは歓声を上げ、粉屋はどこかのお偉方に長い手紙を書く。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os guardas arrombam o cadeado ao meio-dia. As mães comemoram, e o moleiro escreve uma longa carta para alguém importante."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "中午，卫兵砸开了锁。母亲们欢呼起来，磨坊主则给某位大人物写了一封长信。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.miller_hoard.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition miller_hoard: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Haus kauft zum Preis des Müllers und verkauft zu dem des letzten Monats. Odile zuckt bei jedem einzelnen Sack zusammen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The house buys at the miller’s price and sells at last month’s. Odile winces at every single sack."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La casa compra al precio del molinero y vende al del mes pasado. Odile hace una mueca con cada saco."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La maison achète au prix du meunier et revend à celui du mois dernier. Odile grimace à chaque sac."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La casata compra al prezzo del mugnaio e vende a quello del mese scorso. Odile sussulta a ogni singolo sacco."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城は粉屋の値で買い、先月の値で売る。オディールは一袋ごとに顔をしかめる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A casa compra pelo preço do moleiro e vende pelo do mês passado. Odile faz careta a cada saco."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兰腾家照磨坊主的价钱买进，再照上个月的价钱卖出。每过一袋，奥黛尔都要皱一下眉。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.miller_hoard.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition miller_hoard: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Müller verneigt sich tief und hält die Türen verschlossen. Die Mütter stehen stattdessen an der Burgküche an, und Tamsin gehen die Haferflocken aus."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The miller bows deeply and keeps his doors locked. The mothers queue at the castle kitchen instead, and Tamsin runs out of oats."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El molinero hace una profunda reverencia y mantiene las puertas cerradas. Las madres hacen cola en la cocina del castillo, y a Tamsin se le acaba la avena."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le meunier s’incline bien bas et garde ses portes closes. Les mères font plutôt la queue à la cuisine du château, et Tamsin n’a bientôt plus d’avoine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il mugnaio si inchina profondamente e tiene le porte chiuse. Le madri fanno invece la fila alla cucina del castello, e Tamsin resta senza avena."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "粉屋は深々と頭を下げ、戸を閉ざしたままにする。母親たちは代わりに城の台所に列をなし、タムシンの燕麦が底をつく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O moleiro se curva profundamente e mantém as portas trancadas. As mães fazem fila na cozinha do castelo, e a aveia de Tamsin acaba."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "磨坊主深深一躬，照旧锁着门。母亲们只好到城堡厨房门口排队，塔姆辛的燕麦都用光了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.miller_hoard.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition miller_hoard (farmwife): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, der Müller hat sein Mehl weggeschlossen und den Preis verdoppelt, weil, so sagt er, die Düsternis die Mühle holen könnte. Meine Kinder essen Brei aus Hoffnung. Zwingt ihn, seine Türen zu öffnen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, the miller has locked up his flour and doubled the price, because, he says, the Gloom might take the mill. My children eat porridge made of hope. Make him open his doors."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, el molinero ha encerrado su harina y ha doblado el precio porque, según él, la Penumbra podría llevarse el molino. Mis hijos comen gachas de esperanza. Oblíguelo a abrir sus puertas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, le meunier a mis sa farine sous clé et doublé le prix, parce que, dit-il, la Pénombre pourrait prendre le moulin. Mes enfants mangent une bouillie d’espoir. Obligez-le à ouvrir ses portes."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, il mugnaio ha messo sotto chiave la farina e ha raddoppiato il prezzo, perché, dice lui, la Penombra potrebbe prendersi il mulino. I miei figli mangiano pappa di speranza. Obbligatelo ad aprire le porte."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、粉屋が粉をしまい込んで、値を倍にしました。宵闇に水車小屋を取られるかもしれないから、だそうです。うちの子らは、望みで炊いた粥をすすっています。戸を開けさせてください。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, o moleiro trancou a farinha e dobrou o preço, porque, diz ele, a Penumbra pode levar o moinho. Os meus filhos comem mingau de esperança. Obrigue-o a abrir as portas."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，磨坊主把面粉锁起来了，价钱翻了一倍，说是暗霭说不定会把磨坊夺走。我的孩子们吃的是用希望熬的粥。叫他把门打开吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.noble_hunt.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition noble_hunt: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gewährt die Rechte"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Grant the rights"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Conceder los derechos"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Accordez les droits"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Concedete i diritti"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "狩猟権を認める"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os direitos são seus"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "准予狩猎权"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.noble_hunt.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition noble_hunt: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Wild des Tals gehört allen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The valley’s game is for all"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La caza del valle es de todos"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le gibier de la vallée est à tous"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La selvaggina della valle è di tutti"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "谷の獲物は皆のものだ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A caça do vale é de todos"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "河谷的猎物归大家"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.noble_hunt.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition noble_hunt: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vierzig Gold jetzt und bis zum Frühjahr ein Tal voller Wilderer und Groll. Sogar ich ließe das Wild allen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Forty gold now, and a valley of poachers and grudges by spring. Even I would keep the game common."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cuarenta monedas de oro ahora, y para la primavera un valle de cazadores furtivos y rencores. Hasta yo dejaría la caza para todos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quarante pièces d’or maintenant, et d’ici le printemps une vallée pleine de braconniers et de rancunes. Même moi, je laisserais le gibier à tous."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quaranta monete d’oro adesso, e per la primavera una valle di bracconieri e rancori. Perfino io lascerei la selvaggina a tutti."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "今は金貨40枚、春には密猟者と恨みだらけの谷。わたくしでさえ、獲物は皆のものにしておきます。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quarenta moedas de ouro agora, e um vale de caçadores furtivos e rancores até a primavera. Até eu deixaria a caça para todos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "现在得40金币，到开春就是一河谷的偷猎者和怨气。连我都会让猎物归大家。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.noble_hunt.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition noble_hunt: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er geht mit einem Pergament. Bis zum Wochenende werden Bauern bestraft, weil sie auf ihren eigenen Feldern Kaninchen fangen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He leaves with a parchment. By the week’s end, farmers are fined for snaring rabbits on their own fields."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se va con un pergamino. Al acabar la semana, multan a los campesinos por cazar conejos con lazo en sus propios campos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il repart avec un parchemin. À la fin de la semaine, des paysans sont mis à l’amende pour avoir piégé des lapins dans leurs propres champs."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se ne va con una pergamena. Entro fine settimana i contadini vengono multati per aver preso conigli coi lacci nei loro stessi campi."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "男は羊皮紙を手に去る。週の終わりには、自分の畑で兎を罠にかけた農夫たちが、罰金を取られている。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele sai com um pergaminho. No fim da semana, camponeses são multados por pegar coelhos com laço nos próprios campos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他带着一张羊皮纸走了。不到周末，农夫们在自家田里套兔子也要被罚钱了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.noble_hunt.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition noble_hunt: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er geht, ohne sich zu verneigen. In dieser Nacht wird im halben Tal Kaninchen geschmort, und eine Schüssel geht hinauf zur Burg."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He leaves without bowing. That night rabbit stew is cooked in half the valley, and a bowl is sent up to the castle."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se marcha sin inclinarse. Esa noche se guisa conejo en medio valle, y suben una escudilla al castillo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il part sans s’incliner. Ce soir-là, on mijote du lapin dans la moitié de la vallée, et on en fait monter un bol au château."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se ne va senza inchinarsi. Quella notte in mezza valle si cucina stufato di coniglio, e una scodella sale fino al castello."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "男は頭も下げずに去る。その夜、谷の半分で兎の煮込みがつくられ、一杯が城へ届けられる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele sai sem se curvar. Naquela noite, cozinha-se ensopado de coelho em meio vale, e uma tigela sobe até o castelo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他没行礼就走了。那一夜，半个河谷都炖起了兔肉，还有一碗送上了城堡。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.noble_hunt.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition noble_hunt (noble): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, ich spreche für das Haus Oxmoor, das unter Burgherr Aldric die Jagdrechte dieses Tals besaß. Das Haus hätte sie gern zurück. Dafür ein Geschenk von vierzig Gold an Euer Haus und Wildbret für Eure Tafel an jedem Festtag."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, I speak for House Oxmoor, which held the hunting rights of this valley under Lord Aldric. The house should like them back. In return, a gift of forty gold to your house, and venison for your table on every feast day."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, hablo en nombre de la Casa Oxmoor, que tenía los derechos de caza de este valle en tiempos de lord Aldric. A la casa le gustaría recuperarlos. A cambio, un obsequio de cuarenta monedas de oro para su casa, y venado para su mesa en cada día de fiesta."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, je parle pour la maison Oxmoor, qui tenait les droits de chasse de cette vallée sous le seigneur Aldric. La maison aimerait les retrouver. En échange, un don de quarante pièces d’or à votre maison, et du gibier pour votre table à chaque jour de fête."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, parlo a nome di Casa Oxmoor, che sotto Lord Aldric deteneva i diritti di caccia di questa valle. La casata li rivorrebbe. In cambio, un dono di quaranta monete d’oro alla vostra casata, e selvaggina per la vostra tavola in ogni giorno di festa."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、オクスムーア家の名代として参りました。アルドリック様の代に、この谷の狩猟権を持っていた家です。それをお返し願いたい。代わりに、お城へ金貨40枚の贈り物と、祝いの日ごとに鹿肉をお食卓に。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, falo pela Casa Oxmoor, que detinha os direitos de caça deste vale sob o Lorde Aldric. A casa gostaria de tê-los de volta. Em troca, um presente de quarenta moedas de ouro para a sua casa, e carne de caça para a sua mesa em todo dia de festa."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我代表奥克斯穆尔家前来。在奥德里克大人治下，这片河谷的狩猎权归我家所有。我家希望收回。作为回报，赠贵府40金币，每逢节日还为您的餐桌送上鹿肉。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jagt den Dieb"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hunt the thief"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cace al ladrón"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Traquez le voleur"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Date la caccia al ladro"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "盗人を追ってくれ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cace o ladrão"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "查出窃贼"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lasst es gut sein"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Let it go"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Déjelo estar"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Laissez faire"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lasciate perdere"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "見逃そう"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Deixe para lá"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "算了吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zählt noch einmal, Odile"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Count it again, Odile"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cuéntelo otra vez, Odile"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Recomptez, Odile"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ricontate, Odile"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "もう一度数えてくれ、オディール"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Conte de novo, Odile"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "再数一遍，奥黛尔"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ich würde ihn jagen. Aber ein Haus, das seine Schreiber für achtzehn Gold jagt, zählt bald seine Münzen selbst. Lasst es gut sein."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I would hunt him. But a house that hunts its clerks for eighteen gold soon counts its own coins. Let it go."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Yo lo cazaría. Pero una casa que caza a sus escribanos por dieciocho monedas pronto tendrá que contar su dinero ella misma. Déjelo estar."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Moi, je le traquerais. Mais une maison qui traque ses commis pour dix-huit pièces d’or finit par compter elle-même ses sous. Laissez faire."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Io gli darei la caccia. Ma una casata che bracca i suoi scrivani per diciotto monete presto dovrà contarsele da sé. Lasciate perdere."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "わたくしなら追います。ですが、金貨18枚で書記を狩り立てる家は、じきに自分で硬貨を数える羽目になります。見逃してやるのが得策です。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eu o caçaria. Mas uma casa que caça os seus escreventes por dezoito moedas de ouro logo conta as próprias moedas. Deixe para lá."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "换我会查。可为了18金币就追查书记员的家族，很快就得自己数钱了。算了吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.r1a" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: choice 1, it went well.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Es war der Nachtschreiber, der Kerzen für die Kapelle kaufte. Hesper gibt das Gold zurück. Odile bleibt ungerührt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "It was the night clerk, buying candles for the chapel. Hesper gives back the gold. Odile is unmoved."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Era el escribano de noche, que compraba velas para la capilla. Hesper devuelve el oro. Odile no se inmuta."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "C’était le commis de nuit, qui achetait des chandelles pour la chapelle. Hesper rend l’or. Odile reste de marbre."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Era lo scrivano di notte, che comprava candele per la cappella. Hesper restituisce l’oro. Odile resta impassibile."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "夜番の書記が、礼拝堂の蝋燭を買っていたのだった。ヘスパーが金を返す。オディールは眉ひとつ動かさない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Era o escrevente da noite, comprando velas para a capela. Hesper devolve o ouro. Odile não se comove."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "是夜班书记员，拿钱给礼拜堂买了蜡烛。赫斯珀把金币还了回来。奥黛尔不为所动。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.r1b" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: choice 1, it went badly.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Jagd bringt nichts als böses Blut. Drei Schreiber kündigen aus Protest. Das Gold bleibt verschwunden."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The hunt finds nothing but bad feeling. Three clerks resign in protest. The gold stays lost."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La cacería no encuentra más que rencor. Tres escribanos se marchan en protesta. El oro sigue perdido."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La traque ne rapporte que de la rancœur. Trois commis démissionnent en signe de protestation. L’or reste perdu."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La caccia non porta altro che malumore. Tre scrivani si dimettono per protesta. L’oro resta perduto."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "追及で得られたのは、わだかまりだけ。書記が三人、抗議して辞める。金は消えたままだ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A caçada não encontra nada além de mal-estar. Três escreventes se demitem em protesto. O ouro continua sumido."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "追查一无所获，只落下满腹怨气。三名书记员愤而辞职。金币依旧不知去向。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Odile klappt das Kassenbuch mit einem hallenden Knall zu. „Wie {mein Herr|meine Herrin} wünscht.“ Sie wird es wöchentlich erwähnen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Odile closes the ledger with a snap that echoes. “As my {lord|lady} wishes.” She will mention it weekly."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Odile cierra el libro de cuentas con un golpe que resuena. «Como {mi señor|mi señora} desee.» Lo mencionará cada semana."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Odile referme le registre d’un claquement qui résonne. « Comme {monseigneur|madame} voudra. » Elle le rappellera chaque semaine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Odile chiude il libro dei conti con uno schiocco che rimbomba. «Come desidera {il mio signore|la mia signora}.» Ne parlerà ogni settimana."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "オディールは帳簿をばたんと閉じ、その音が響く。「城主様のお望みのままに」。この件は毎週、話に出ることになる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Odile fecha o livro-caixa com um estalo que ecoa. “Como {o meu senhor|a minha senhora} desejar.” Ela vai mencionar isso toda semana."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "奥黛尔啪地合上账簿，声音在大厅里回荡。“大人说了算。”此后她每周都会提一次。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sie zählt noch einmal, langsam, vor Euren Augen. Es fehlen achtzehn Gold. Zweimal."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She counts again, slowly, in front of you. It is eighteen gold short. Twice."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vuelve a contar, despacio, delante de usted. Faltan dieciocho monedas de oro. Dos veces."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Elle recompte, lentement, sous vos yeux. Il manque dix-huit pièces d’or. Deux fois."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Riconta, piano, davanti a voi. Mancano diciotto monete d’oro. Due volte."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "オディールは目の前で、ゆっくりと数え直す。金貨18枚足りない。二度数えても。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ela conta de novo, devagar, na sua frente. Faltam dezoito moedas de ouro. Duas vezes."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "她当着你的面，慢慢又数了一遍。少18金币。两遍都是。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.odile_ledger.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition odile_ledger (odile): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mein Herr|Meine Herrin}, in der Schatzkammer fehlen achtzehn Gold, und mein Kassenbuch irrt nie. Entweder stiehlt ein Schreiber, oder Pip hat zählen gelernt. Ich kann den Dieb in aller Stille jagen, aber eine Jagd kostet Freunde."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, the treasury is eighteen gold short, and my ledger is never wrong. Either a clerk is stealing, or Pip has learned to count. I can hunt the thief quietly, but a hunt costs friends."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, al tesoro le faltan dieciocho monedas de oro, y mi libro de cuentas nunca se equivoca. O un escribano está robando, o Pip ha aprendido a contar. Puedo cazar al ladrón con discreción, pero una cacería cuesta amigos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, il manque dix-huit pièces d’or au trésor, et mon registre ne se trompe jamais. Soit un commis vole, soit Pip a appris à compter. Je peux traquer le voleur discrètement, mais une traque coûte des amis."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, al tesoro mancano diciotto monete d’oro, e il mio libro dei conti non sbaglia mai. O uno scrivano ruba, o Pip ha imparato a contare. Posso dare la caccia al ladro in silenzio, ma una caccia costa amici."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、金庫が金貨18枚足りません。わたくしの帳簿に間違いはございません。書記が盗んでいるか、ピップが数を覚えたかです。盗人は内密に追えますが、追えば友を失います。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, faltam dezoito moedas de ouro no tesouro, e o meu livro-caixa nunca erra. Ou um escrevente está roubando, ou Pip aprendeu a contar. Posso caçar o ladrão em silêncio, mas uma caçada custa amigos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "大人，府库少了18金币，而我的账簿从不出错。要么是哪个书记员在偷，要么是皮普学会了数数。我可以悄悄追查窃贼，可一追查，就要失去朋友。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.old_sergeant.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition old_sergeant: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Willkommen zurück, Feldwebel"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Welcome back, sergeant"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bienvenido otra vez, sargento"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bon retour, sergent"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bentornato, sergente"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "よく戻った、軍曹"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bem-vindo de volta, sargento"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "欢迎归队，军士"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.old_sergeant.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition old_sergeant: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Schont Eure Knie, alter Freund"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rest your knees, old friend"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Descanse esas rodillas, viejo amigo"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ménagez vos genoux, vieil ami"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Riposate le ginocchia, vecchio amico"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "膝をいたわってくれ、古なじみ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Poupe os joelhos, velho amigo"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "歇歇膝盖吧，老伙计"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.old_sergeant.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition old_sergeant: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein alter Soldat am Tor ist zwei junge wert. Nehmt ihn."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An old soldier at the gate is worth two young ones. Take him."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un soldado viejo en la puerta vale por dos jóvenes. Acéptelo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un vieux soldat à la porte en vaut deux jeunes. Prenez-le."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un vecchio soldato alla porta ne vale due giovani. Prendetelo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "門に立つ古参兵ひとりは、若いの二人に値します。雇わぬ手はございません。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Um soldado velho no portão vale dois jovens. Aceite-o."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "门口一个老兵，抵得上两个新兵。收下他。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.old_sergeant.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition old_sergeant: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er salutiert so heftig, dass sein Helm klingt. Brannock tut so, als freue er sich nicht."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He salutes so hard his helmet rings. Brannock pretends not to be glad."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Saluda con tanto brío que le suena el yelmo. Brannock finge que no se alegra."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il salue si fort que son casque sonne. Brannock fait semblant de ne pas être content."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Saluta così forte che l’elmo gli risuona. Brannock finge di non esserne contento."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兜が鳴るほどの勢いで敬礼する。ブラノックは、嬉しくないふりをする。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele bate continência com tanta força que o elmo retine. Brannock finge que não está contente."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他敬礼敬得太猛，头盔都嗡地一响。布兰诺克装作并不高兴。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.old_sergeant.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition old_sergeant: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Er verneigt sich, ein wenig steif. Später hört Ihr ihn in der Küche sagen, {der neue Herr|die neue Herrin} habe ein gütiges Gesicht."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "He bows, a little stiffly. Later you hear him tell the kitchen the new {lord|lady} has a kind face."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se inclina, algo rígido. Más tarde lo oye decir en la cocina que {el nuevo señor|la nueva señora} tiene cara de buena persona."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il s’incline, un peu raide. Plus tard, vous l’entendez dire à la cuisine que {le nouveau seigneur|la nouvelle dame} a l’air {bon|bonne}."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Si inchina, un po’ rigido. Più tardi lo sentite dire in cucina che {il nuovo signore|la nuova signora} ha un viso buono."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "軍曹は少しぎこちなく頭を下げる。あとで、新しい城主様は優しい顔をしておられる、と台所で話しているのが聞こえる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ele se curva, um pouco rígido. Mais tarde, você o ouve dizer na cozinha que {o novo senhor|a nova senhora} tem um rosto bondoso."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "他鞠了一躬，有些僵硬。后来你听见他在厨房里说，新城主长着一张和善的脸。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.old_sergeant.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition old_sergeant (soldier): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ich habe zwanzig Winter das Tor des alten Herrn gehalten. Meine Knie sind hin, mein Arm nicht. Gebt mir einen Speer und einen Platz am Tor, und ich verlange keinen Lohn außer Suppe."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I held the old lord’s gate for twenty winters. My knees are done, my arm is not. Give me a spear and a place by the gate, and I ask no pay but soup."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Guardé la puerta del viejo señor durante veinte inviernos. Las rodillas ya no me dan, el brazo sí. Deme una lanza y un puesto junto a la puerta, y no pido más paga que la sopa."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "J’ai tenu la porte de l’ancien seigneur pendant vingt hivers. Mes genoux sont usés, mon bras, non. Donnez-moi une lance et une place près de la porte, et je ne demande pour solde que de la soupe."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ho tenuto la porta del vecchio signore per venti inverni. Le ginocchia sono andate, il braccio no. Datemi una lancia e un posto vicino alla porta, e come paga chiedo solo la zuppa."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "先代の城主様の門を、二十の冬、守りました。膝はもうだめですが、腕はまだ利きます。槍を一本と、門の脇に持ち場をください。給金はいりません。スープさえいただければ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Guardei o portão do velho senhor por vinte invernos. Os joelhos estão acabados, o braço não. Me dê uma lança e um lugar junto ao portão, e não peço pagamento além de sopa."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "我替老城主守了二十个冬天的城门。膝盖不行了，胳膊还行。给我一杆长矛，在城门边给我个位置，我不要军饷，只要一碗汤。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Lampe bleibt. Keine Unterschrift."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Keep the lamp. Sign nothing."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Me quedo con la lámpara. No firmo nada."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Je garde la lampe. Je ne signe rien."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tengo la lampada. Non firmo niente."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ランプは受け取る。署名はしない"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fico com o candeeiro. Sem assinatura."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "灯留下。不签字。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Unterschreiben."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sign."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Firmo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Je signe."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Firmare."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "署名する"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Assinar."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "签。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Beides zurück, mit Dank."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Send both back, kindly."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Devuelvo las dos cosas, con cortesía."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Je rends les deux, avec courtoisie."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Rendete entrambi, con garbo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "どちらも、丁重にお返しする"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Devolva os dois, com cortesia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "都退回去，道个谢。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein Geschenk mit einem Papier darunter ist eine Schuld. Behaltet die Lampe, {mein Herr|meine Herrin}. Von Lampen verstehen wir etwas. Unterschreibt nichts."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A gift with a paper under it is a debt. Keep the lamp, my {lord|lady}. Lamps we understand. Sign nothing."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un regalo con un papel debajo es una deuda. Quédese con la lámpara, {mi señor|mi señora}. De lámparas sabemos. No firme nada."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un cadeau avec un papier dessous, c’est une dette. Gardez la lampe, {monseigneur|madame}. Les lampes, nous connaissons. Ne signez rien."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un dono con sotto una carta è un debito. Tenete la lampada, {mio signore|mia signora}. Di lampade ce ne intendiamo. Non firmate niente."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "書面を下に敷いた贈り物は、借金です。ランプはお受け取りを、城主様。灯りのことなら心得ております。署名は、ひとつもなさらぬよう。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Presente com papel embaixo é dívida. Fique com o candeeiro, {meu senhor|minha senhora}. De candeeiros nós entendemos. Não assine nada."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "底下压着文书的礼物，就是债。灯留下，大人。灯我们懂。什么都别签。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pell verneigt sich, als hätte er genau das erhofft. Odile trägt die Lampe am ausgestreckten Arm hinaus und zählt ihr Silber zweimal."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pell bows as if this were the answer he had hoped for. Odile carries the lamp out at arm’s length and counts its silver twice."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pell se inclina como si esa fuera la respuesta que esperaba. Odile se lleva la lámpara con el brazo extendido y cuenta su plata dos veces."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pell s’incline comme si c’était la réponse qu’il espérait. Odile emporte la lampe à bout de bras et compte son argent deux fois."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pell si inchina come se fosse proprio la risposta sperata. Odile porta fuori la lampada a braccio teso e ne conta l’argento due volte."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ペルは、それこそ望んでいた答えだと言わんばかりに一礼する。オディールはランプを腕いっぱいに遠ざけて運び出し、銀を二度数える。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pell se curva como se fosse exatamente a resposta que esperava. Odile leva o candeeiro para fora com o braço esticado e conta a prata dele duas vezes."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "佩尔躬身行礼，仿佛这正是他盼望的答复。奥黛尔伸直手臂把灯拿出去，把灯上的银子掂量了两遍。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dreißig Gold auf dem Tisch, noch warm von seiner Hand. Pell löscht Euren Namen mit großer Sorgfalt ab. Odile sagt den Rest des Tages kein Wort."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Thirty gold on the table, still warm from his hand. Pell blots your name with great care. Odile says nothing for the rest of the day."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Treinta monedas de oro sobre la mesa, aún tibias de su mano. Pell seca la tinta de su nombre con sumo cuidado. Odile no dice nada en todo el día."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Trente pièces d’or sur la table, encore tièdes de sa main. Pell passe le buvard sur votre nom avec grand soin. Odile ne dit plus rien de la journée."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Trenta monete d’oro sul tavolo, ancora calde della sua mano. Pell asciuga l’inchiostro del vostro nome con gran cura. Odile non dice una parola per il resto del giorno."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "卓の上に金貨30枚。まだ彼の手の温もりが残っている。ペルは署名に、ことのほか丁寧に吸い取り紙を当てる。オディールはその日、最後までひと言も口をきかない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Trinta moedas de ouro na mesa, ainda mornas da mão dele. Pell passa o mata-borrão no seu nome com todo o cuidado. Odile não diz nada pelo resto do dia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "30金币摆在桌上，还带着他手心的温度。佩尔小心翼翼地吸干你名字上的墨。奥黛尔一整天没再说话。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "„Goldenacre wird sich dieser Höflichkeit erinnern“, sagt Pell und lächelt mit allen Zähnen. Odile bringt ihn selbst bis ans Tor."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“Goldenacre will remember the courtesy,” says Pell, smiling with every tooth. Odile walks him to the gate herself."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Goldenacre recordará la cortesía», dice Pell, sonriendo con todos los dientes. Odile en persona lo acompaña hasta la puerta."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "« Goldenacre se souviendra de cette courtoisie », dit Pell en souriant de toutes ses dents. Odile le raccompagne elle-même jusqu’à la porte."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Goldenacre ricorderà la cortesia», dice Pell, sorridendo con tutti i denti. Odile lo accompagna di persona alla porta."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "「ゴールデンエーカーは、このご丁重を忘れますまい」と、ペルは歯を一本残らず見せて笑う。オディールが自ら、門まで見送る。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“Goldenacre há de se lembrar da cortesia”, diz Pell, sorrindo com todos os dentes. Odile o acompanha pessoalmente até o portão."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“戈尔登埃克会记住这份礼数。”佩尔说着，露出满口的牙笑了。奥黛尔亲自送他到门口。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.oxmoor_gift.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition oxmoor_gift (lorenzPell, story days 5-6): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lorenz Pell, Verwalter der Lady Petra Oxmoor von Goldenacre. Meine Herrin schickt eine Silberlampe für Eure Tafel, {Lord|Lady} Lantern, und ein kleines Papier: dreißig Gold noch heute, geliehen auf das Tal. Eine Förmlichkeit unter Freunden. Die Feder ist schon eingetaucht."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lorenz Pell, steward to Lady Petra Oxmoor of Goldenacre. My lady sends a silver lamp for your table, {Lord|Lady} Lantern, and one small paper: thirty gold today, lent against the valley. A formality between friends. The pen is already inked."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lorenz Pell, mayordomo de lady Petra Oxmoor de Goldenacre. Mi señora envía una lámpara de plata para su mesa, {lord|lady} Lantern, y un papelito: treinta monedas de oro hoy mismo, prestadas sobre el valle. Una formalidad entre amigos. La pluma ya está entintada."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lorenz Pell, intendant de dame Petra Oxmoor, de Goldenacre. Madame envoie une lampe d’argent pour votre table, {seigneur|dame} Lantern, et un petit papier : trente pièces d’or aujourd’hui, gagées sur la vallée. Une formalité entre amis. La plume est déjà dans l’encre."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lorenz Pell, intendente di Lady Petra Oxmoor di Goldenacre. La mia signora manda una lampada d’argento per la vostra tavola, {Lord|Lady} Lantern, e una piccola carta: trenta monete d’oro oggi stesso, in prestito, con la valle in pegno. Una formalità tra amici. La penna è già intinta."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ゴールデンエーカーのペトラ・オクスムーア様に仕える執事、ローレンツ・ペルでございます。我が主より、お食卓に銀のランプを、ランタン様。それと小さな書面を一枚。本日金貨30枚を、谷を担保にお貸しいたします。友人同士の形ばかりの手続き。羽根筆は、もう墨に浸してございます。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Lorenz Pell, intendente de Lady Petra Oxmoor de Goldenacre. A minha senhora envia um candeeiro de prata para a sua mesa, {Lorde|Lady} Lantern, e um papelzinho: trinta moedas de ouro hoje, com o vale como garantia. Mera formalidade entre amigos. A pena já está molhada."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "我是洛伦茨·佩尔，戈尔登埃克的佩特拉·奥克斯穆尔大人的管家。我家主人送来一盏银灯，供您餐桌之用，兰腾大人，另附一纸小小的文书：今日借您30金币，以河谷作保。朋友之间的手续而已。笔已蘸好了墨。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Herein, gegen Gebühr"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Let them in, for a fee"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que entren, pagando"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Qu’ils entrent, contre une obole"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Entrino, a pagamento"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "入れましょう。お代はいただきます"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que entrem, pagando"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "收费放行"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Herein, umsonst"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Let them in freely"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que entren, sin pagar"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Qu’ils entrent librement"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Entrino, gratis"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "お代なしで、入れましょう"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Que entrem de graça"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "免费放行"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Tor bleibt den Unseren"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The gate is for our own"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La puerta es para los nuestros"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La porte est pour les nôtres"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La porta è per i nostri"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "門は身内のためのものです"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O portão é para os nossos"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城门只为自己人开"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Glaube, der Eintritt zahlt, bleibt Glaube. Und er zahlt. Lasst sie herein, für eine Münze pro Kopf."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Faith that pays an entry fee is still faith. And it pays. Let them in, for a coin each."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La fe que paga entrada sigue siendo fe. Y paga. Déjelos entrar, a una moneda por cabeza."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Une foi qui paie son entrée reste une foi. Et elle paie. Faites-les entrer, une pièce par tête."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una fede che paga l’ingresso è pur sempre fede. E paga. Fateli entrare, una moneta a testa."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "入場料を払う信心も、信心には変わりません。しかも払うのです。お入れなさいませ。一人につき硬貨一枚で。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fé que paga entrada continua sendo fé. E paga. Deixe-os entrar, por uma moeda cada um."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "交了入场费的信仰，仍是信仰。何况它还付钱。让他们进来，每人一枚钱币。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Pilger füllen die Kapelle und die Schatzkammer. Die Stadt murrt über das Gedränge und verkauft ihnen alles, was sie hat."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The pilgrims fill the chapel and the treasury. The town grumbles about crowds and sells them everything it owns."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los peregrinos llenan la capilla y el tesoro. El pueblo se queja del gentío y les vende todo lo que tiene."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les pèlerins remplissent la chapelle et le trésor. La ville se plaint de la foule et leur vend tout ce qu’elle possède."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I pellegrini riempiono la cappella e il tesoro. Il borgo brontola per la ressa e vende loro tutto quello che ha."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "巡礼たちは礼拝堂と金庫を満たす。町は人ごみに文句を言い、持っている物を何でも彼らに売りつける。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os peregrinos enchem a capela e o tesouro. A cidade reclama da multidão e lhes vende tudo o que tem."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "朝圣者挤满了礼拜堂，也填满了府库。镇上的人抱怨人多，却把家里能卖的都卖给了他们。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Pilger beten, weinen und legen Blumen am Tor nieder. Irgendwie fühlt sich der Saal einen Tag lang heiliger an."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The pilgrims pray, weep and leave flowers at the gate. Somehow the hall feels holier for a day."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los peregrinos rezan, lloran y dejan flores en la puerta. De algún modo, el salón parece más sagrado durante un día."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les pèlerins prient, pleurent et laissent des fleurs à la porte. Sans qu’on sache pourquoi, la salle paraît plus sainte toute une journée."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I pellegrini pregano, piangono e lasciano fiori alla porta. Chissà come, per un giorno il salone sembra più sacro."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "巡礼たちは祈り、泣き、門に花を手向ける。なぜか大広間が、一日だけ神聖になったように感じられる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os peregrinos rezam, choram e deixam flores no portão. De algum modo, o salão parece mais sagrado por um dia."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "朝圣者祈祷、流泪，在城门边放下鲜花。不知怎的，大厅那一天显得格外神圣。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Pilger knien stattdessen vor dem Tor und beten dort die ganze Nacht. Die Wachen finden das unheimlich."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The pilgrims kneel outside the gate instead and pray there all night. The guards find it unsettling."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los peregrinos se arrodillan entonces ante la puerta y rezan allí toda la noche. A los guardias les inquieta."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les pèlerins s’agenouillent plutôt devant la porte et y prient toute la nuit. Les gardes trouvent cela inquiétant."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I pellegrini si inginocchiano invece fuori dalla porta e pregano lì tutta la notte. Le guardie lo trovano inquietante."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "巡礼たちは代わりに門の外でひざまずき、夜通しそこで祈る。衛兵たちは落ち着かない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Os peregrinos se ajoelham do lado de fora do portão e rezam ali a noite toda. Os guardas acham isso inquietante."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "朝圣者便跪在城门外，在那里祈祷了一整夜。卫兵们觉得心里发毛。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pilgrims.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pilgrims (widow, endless only): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, Pilger sind aus drei Tälern weit gekommen, um die Burg zu sehen, die die Düsternis aufhält, und die Flamme, die nie erlischt. Sie würden zahlen, um in der Kapelle zu beten. Oder das Tor bleibt den Unseren."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, pilgrims have come from three valleys away to see the castle that holds back the Gloom and the Flame that never goes out. They would pay to pray in the chapel. Or we keep the gate for our own."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, han venido peregrinos desde tres valles más allá para ver el castillo que contiene a la Penumbra y la Llama que nunca se apaga. Pagarían por rezar en la capilla. O dejamos la puerta para los nuestros."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, des pèlerins sont venus de trois vallées plus loin pour voir le château qui retient la Pénombre et la Flamme qui ne s’éteint jamais. Ils paieraient pour prier à la chapelle. Ou nous gardons la porte pour les nôtres."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, sono arrivati pellegrini da tre valli più in là per vedere il castello che trattiene la Penombra e la Fiamma che non si spegne mai. Pagherebbero per pregare in cappella. Oppure teniamo la porta per i nostri."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、三つ向こうの谷から巡礼が来ております。宵闇を食い止める城と、決して消えない炎を見たいと。礼拝堂で祈るためなら、お金を払うそうです。あるいは、門は身内のためだけにしておくか。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, vieram peregrinos de três vales de distância para ver o castelo que segura a Penumbra e a Chama que nunca se apaga. Pagariam para rezar na capela. Ou guardamos o portão para os nossos."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，有朝圣者从三道河谷外赶来，想看看挡住暗霭的城堡，和永不熄灭的圣焰。他们愿意出钱到礼拜堂祈祷。要么，城门只为自己人开。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_farewell.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_farewell: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Erzähl ihn, Pip"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tell it, Pip"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cuéntalo, Pip"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Raconte-la, Pip"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Raccontala, Pip"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "聞かせて、ピップ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pode contar, Pip"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "讲吧，皮普"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_farewell.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_farewell: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Heb ihn für danach auf"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Save it for after"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Guárdalo para después"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Garde-la pour après"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tienila per dopo"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "戦いの後まで取っておいて"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Guarde para depois"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "留到以后再讲"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_farewell.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_farewell: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wenn wir morgen sterben, dann lieber lachend. Sagt ihm nicht, dass ich das gesagt habe."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If we die tomorrow, I would rather do it laughing. Do not tell him I said so."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Si mañana morimos, prefiero hacerlo riendo. No le diga que lo dije."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Si nous devons mourir demain, j’aime autant que ce soit en riant. Ne lui dites pas que je l’ai dit."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se domani dobbiamo morire, preferisco farlo ridendo. Non ditegli che l’ho detto."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "明日死ぬのなら、笑いながらのほうがいい。わたくしがそう申したとは、あの者に言わないでくださいませ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se morrermos amanhã, prefiro que seja rindo. Não conte a ele que eu disse isso."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "要是明天就死，我宁愿笑着死。别告诉他这话是我说的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_farewell.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_farewell: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "„Aldric wettete, kein Narr bringe diesen Saal vor der Schlacht zum Lachen. Zahlt, Aldric!“ Der Saal tobt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“Aldric bet me a gold piece no fool could make this hall laugh before a battle. Pay up, Aldric.” The hall roars."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Cuando Odile leyó el nombre en el libro de familia, toda la corte se volvió a mirar la escalera.» El salón estalla en carcajadas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "« Quand Odile a lu le nom dans le livre de famille, toute la cour a regardé l’échelle. » La salle éclate de rire."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Quando Odile lesse il nome dal libro di famiglia, tutta la corte guardò la scala.» Il salone scoppia a ridere."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "「オディールが家系の書からその名を読み上げたとき、城の者がそろって梯子を見たのです」。大広間がどっと沸く。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“Quando Odile leu o nome no livro da família, a corte inteira olhou para a escada.” O salão vem abaixo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“奥黛尔从家谱里念出那个名字时，城堡里上上下下都扭头去看那把梯子。”大厅里哄堂大笑。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_farewell.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_farewell: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip grinst. „Dann müssen wir eben leben, Eure Dochtheit. Ich weigere mich, ihn zu verschwenden.“ Er jongliert drei Äpfel aus dem Saal."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip grins. “Then we have to live, Your Wickship. I refuse to waste it.” He juggles three apples out of the hall."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip sonríe de oreja a oreja. «Entonces tendremos que vivir, Su Mechencia. Me niego a desperdiciarlo.» Sale del salón haciendo malabares con tres manzanas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip sourit jusqu’aux oreilles. « Alors il faudra vivre, Votre Lumignence. Je refuse de la gâcher. » Il sort de la salle en jonglant avec trois pommes."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip sogghigna. «Allora ci tocca vivere, Vostra Stoppinenza. Mi rifiuto di sprecarla.» Esce dal salone facendo il giocoliere con tre mele."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ピップはにやりと笑う。「では、生き延びねばなりませんな、灯心閣下。無駄にするのはごめんです」。林檎を三つお手玉しながら、大広間を出ていく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip sorri de orelha a orelha. “Então vamos ter de viver, Vossa Paviência. Eu me recuso a desperdiçá-la.” Sai do salão fazendo malabarismo com três maçãs."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "皮普咧嘴一笑。“那我们就非活下去不可了，灯芯阁下。小的可不肯糟蹋了它。”他一路抛接着三个苹果出了大厅。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_farewell.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_farewell (pip, story day 19): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eure Dochtheit, morgen kommt der Lichtlose König, und ich habe meinen besten Witz noch nicht erzählt. Sterben wir alle, stirbt er mit uns, und das wäre die eigentliche Tragödie. Darf ich ihn jetzt erzählen, vor dem ganzen Saal?"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Wickship, tomorrow the Lightless King comes, and I have not yet told my best joke. If we all die, it dies with us, and that would be the real tragedy. May I tell it now, to the whole hall?"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Su Mechencia, mañana viene el Rey sin Luz, y aún no he contado mi mejor chiste. Si morimos todos, morirá con nosotros, y esa sería la verdadera tragedia. ¿Puedo contarlo ahora, ante todo el salón?"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Votre Lumignence, demain vient le Roi sans lumière, et je n’ai pas encore raconté ma meilleure blague. Si nous mourons tous, elle meurt avec nous, et ce serait là la vraie tragédie. Puis-je la raconter maintenant, devant toute la salle ?"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vostra Stoppinenza, domani arriva il Re senza Luce, e io non ho ancora raccontato la mia battuta migliore. Se moriamo tutti, muore con noi, e quella sì che sarebbe una tragedia. Posso raccontarla adesso, a tutto il salone?"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "灯心閣下、明日は光なき王がやってまいります。なのにわたくしめは、とっておきの冗談をまだ披露しておりません。皆が死ねば冗談も道連れ、それこそ本当の悲劇でございます。今ここで、大広間の皆に話してもよろしいでしょうか。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vossa Paviência, amanhã chega o Rei sem Luz, e eu ainda não contei a minha melhor piada. Se todos nós morrermos, ela morre conosco, e essa seria a verdadeira tragédia. Posso contá-la agora, para o salão inteiro?"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "灯芯阁下，明天无光之王就要来了，可小的最好的笑话还没讲。要是我们都死了，它也跟着死，那才是真正的悲剧。小的现在能讲给整个大厅听吗？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gewährt, Herr Minister"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Granted, Minister"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Concedido, señor ministro"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Accordé, monsieur le ministre"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Concesso, signor ministro"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "認めよう、大臣"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Concedido, senhor ministro"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "准了，大臣"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hut und Siegel, kein Kuchen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hat and seal, no cake"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sombrero y sello, sin pastel"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chapeau et sceau, pas de gâteau"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cappello e sigillo, niente torta"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "帽子と印章だけ。菓子はなし"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Chapéu e selo, sem bolo"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "帽子和印章，没有蛋糕"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Narren brauchen kein Ministerium"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fools need no ministry"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Los bufones no necesitan ministerio"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pas de ministère pour un bouffon"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ai giullari non servono ministeri"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "道化に省は要らない"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bobo não precisa de ministério"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "弄臣不需要官职"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gebt ihm den Hut und das Siegel. Bekommt er Kuchen, will er bald einen Haushalt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Give him the hat and the seal. If he gets cake, he will want a budget."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dele el sombrero y el sello. Si le da pastel, querrá un presupuesto."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Donnez-lui le chapeau et le sceau. S’il a du gâteau, il voudra un budget."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dategli il cappello e il sigillo. Se ottiene la torta, vorrà un bilancio."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "帽子と印章は、くれておやりなさいませ。焼き菓子まで与えたら、次は予算を欲しがります。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dê a ele o chapéu e o selo. Se ganhar bolo, vai querer um orçamento."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "帽子和印章给他。要是给了蛋糕，他就要预算了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pips erster Erlass verbietet das Stirnrunzeln an Markttagen. Alle ignorieren ihn, was laut Pip beweist, dass das Gesetz wirkt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip’s first decree bans frowning on market days. Everyone ignores it, which Pip says proves the law is working."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El primer decreto de Pip prohíbe fruncir el ceño los días de mercado. Nadie le hace caso, lo cual, según Pip, demuestra que la ley funciona."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le premier décret de Pip interdit de froncer les sourcils les jours de marché. Tout le monde l’ignore, ce qui, selon Pip, prouve que la loi fonctionne."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il primo decreto di Pip vieta di aggrottare la fronte nei giorni di mercato. Tutti lo ignorano, il che, dice Pip, dimostra che la legge funziona."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ピップの最初の布告は、市の立つ日のしかめ面を禁じる。誰も守らないが、ピップに言わせれば、それこそ法が効いている証拠だ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "O primeiro decreto de Pip proíbe cara fechada em dia de feira. Todos o ignoram, o que, segundo Pip, prova que a lei funciona."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "皮普的第一道法令：集市日禁止皱眉。人人都当没听见，皮普说这恰好证明法令奏效了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip nimmt würdevoll an und siegelt sofort Odiles Kassenbuch mit einem Marmeladenstempel. Odiles Antwort ist nicht überliefert."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip accepts with dignity and at once seals Odile’s ledger with a jam stamp. Odile’s reply is not recorded."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip acepta con dignidad y enseguida sella el libro de cuentas de Odile con un sello de mermelada. La respuesta de Odile no consta en ningún registro."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip accepte avec dignité et scelle aussitôt le registre d’Odile d’un cachet de confiture. La réponse d’Odile n’a pas été consignée."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip accetta con dignità e subito sigilla il libro dei conti di Odile con un timbro di marmellata. La risposta di Odile non è stata messa agli atti."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ピップは威厳をもって拝受し、さっそくオディールの帳簿にジャムで封印を押す。オディールの返答は、記録に残っていない。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip aceita com dignidade e na mesma hora sela o livro-caixa de Odile com um carimbo de geleia. A resposta de Odile não ficou registrada."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "皮普郑重地接受了，随即用果酱戳子在奥黛尔的账簿上盖了个章。奥黛尔如何回应，编年史上没有记载。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip verneigt sich so tief, dass seine Schellen den Boden berühren. „{Ein weiser Herr|Eine weise Herrin}“, sagt er. „Weise und kein bisschen lustig.“"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip bows so low his bells touch the floor. “A wise {lord|lady},” he says. “Wise, and not one bit funny.”"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip se inclina tanto que sus cascabeles tocan el suelo. «{Un señor sabio|Una señora sabia}», dice. «{Sabio|Sabia}, y ni pizca de {gracioso|graciosa}.»"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip s’incline si bas que ses grelots touchent le sol. « {Un seigneur|Une dame} bien sage, dit-il. Sage, et pas drôle pour un sou. »"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip si inchina così in basso che i suoi sonagli toccano il pavimento. «{Un signore saggio|Una signora saggia}», dice. «{Saggio|Saggia}, e per niente divertente.»"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ピップは鈴が床に触れるほど深く頭を下げる。「賢明な城主様でございます」と言う。「賢明で、ちっとも面白くない」"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pip se curva tanto que os guizos tocam o chão. “{Um senhor sábio|Uma senhora sábia}”, diz ele. “{Sábio|Sábia}, e nem um pouco {engraçado|engraçada}.”"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "皮普深深一躬，帽上的铃铛碰到了地面。“英明的城主，”他说，“英明，而且一点也不好笑。”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pip_minister.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pip_minister (pip): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eure Dochtheit, jeder Hof hat Minister. Odile hat die Schatzkammer, Brannock die Mauern, Hesper die Flamme. Ich bitte darum, Minister für Witze zu werden, mit Hut, Siegel und einem Lohn von einem Kupfer und einem Kuchen pro Woche."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your Wickship, every court has ministers. Odile has the treasury, Brannock the walls, Hesper the Flame. I ask to be Minister of Jokes, with a hat, a seal and a salary of one copper and one cake a week."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Su Mechencia, toda corte tiene ministros. Odile tiene el tesoro; Brannock, las murallas; Hesper, la Llama. Pido ser ministro de Chistes, con sombrero, sello y un sueldo de un cobre y un pastel a la semana."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Votre Lumignence, toute cour a ses ministres. Odile a le trésor, Brannock les murailles, Hesper la Flamme. Je demande à être ministre des Blagues, avec un chapeau, un sceau et un traitement d’un sou et d’un gâteau par semaine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vostra Stoppinenza, ogni corte ha i suoi ministri. Odile ha il tesoro, Brannock le mura, Hesper la Fiamma. Chiedo di essere nominato ministro delle Battute, con cappello, sigillo e uno stipendio di un soldo e una torta alla settimana."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "灯心閣下、どの城にも大臣がおります。オディールは金庫、ブラノックは城壁、ヘスパーは炎。わたくしめは、冗談大臣を拝命したく存じます。帽子と印章と、週に銅貨1枚と焼き菓子ひとつの俸給つきで。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Vossa Paviência, toda corte tem ministros. Odile tem o tesouro, Brannock as muralhas, Hesper a Chama. Peço para ser ministro das Piadas, com chapéu, selo e um salário de um tostão e um bolo por semana."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "灯芯阁下，哪座城堡没有几位大臣？奥黛尔管府库，布兰诺克管城墙，赫斯珀管圣焰。小的请求出任笑话大臣，配一顶帽子、一枚印章，薪俸每周一个铜板外加一块蛋糕。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.pitch_trap.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition pitch_trap: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Versucht es mit Teer"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Try the tar"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
