          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_garden.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_garden: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nesseln geben gute Suppe"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Nettles make good soup"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Las ortigas dan buena sopa"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les orties font une bonne soupe"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le ortiche fanno una buona zuppa"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "いらくさは、いいスープになります"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Urtiga dá uma boa sopa"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "荨麻能煮好汤"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_garden.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_garden: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Blumen erfreuen das Auge. Kräuter erfreuen die Kräuterfrau, die weniger verlangt, wenn sie selbst anbaut. Pflanzt Kräuter."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Flowers please the eye. Herbs please the herb-wife, who charges less when she grows her own. Plant herbs."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Las flores alegran la vista. Las hierbas alegran a la herbolaria, que cobra menos cuando cultiva las suyas. Plante hierbas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les fleurs plaisent à l’œil. Les herbes plaisent à la guérisseuse, qui demande moins cher quand elle cultive les siennes. Plantez des herbes."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I fiori rallegrano l’occhio. Le erbe rallegrano la donna delle erbe, che chiede meno quando le coltiva da sé. Piantate erbe medicinali."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "花は目を楽しませます。薬草は薬草師を喜ばせ、自分で育てればお代も下がります。薬草に決まっております。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Flores agradam aos olhos. Ervas agradam à erveira, que cobra menos quando planta as próprias. Plante ervas."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "花悦人眼。草药悦草药婆，她自己种了药，收价就低。种草药吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_garden.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_garden: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Kinder pflanzen erst alles verkehrt herum. Eine Woche später stehen Blumen in Kästen und Bohnen in Reihen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The children plant everything upside down at first. A week later there are flowers in boxes and beans in rows."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al principio los niños lo plantan todo al revés. Una semana después hay flores en jardineras y habas en hileras."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les enfants plantent tout à l’envers, d’abord. Une semaine plus tard, il y a des fleurs dans les caisses et des fèves en rangs."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "All’inizio i bambini piantano tutto a testa in giù. Una settimana dopo ci sono fiori nelle cassette e fagioli in fila."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもたちは最初、何もかも逆さまに植える。一週間後には、箱に花が咲き、畝に豆が並ぶ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No começo, as crianças plantam tudo de cabeça para baixo. Uma semana depois, há flores em caixotes e feijões em fileiras."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子们起初把什么都种倒了。一周后，花开满了花箱，豆子排成了行。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_garden.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_garden: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Weide, Salbei und Minze wachsen, wo die Nesseln standen. Die Kräuterfrau kommt täglich und tut, als wäre sie nicht dankbar."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Willow, sage and mint grow where the nettles were. The herb-wife visits daily and pretends she is not grateful."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sauce, salvia y menta crecen donde había ortigas. La herbolaria viene a diario y finge no estar agradecida."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le saule, la sauge et la menthe poussent là où étaient les orties. La guérisseuse passe chaque jour et fait semblant de ne pas être reconnaissante."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Salice, salvia e menta crescono dove c’erano le ortiche. La donna delle erbe passa ogni giorno e finge di non essere grata."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "いらくさのあった所に、柳とセージと薄荷が育つ。薬草師の女は毎日やって来て、ありがたくなどないふりをする。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Salgueiro, sálvia e hortelã crescem onde havia urtigas. A erveira aparece todo dia e finge que não está grata."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "荨麻长过的地方，长出了柳树、鼠尾草和薄荷。草药婆天天来，装作并不感激。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_garden.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_garden: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sie lacht, ein wenig. „Das hat er auch immer gesagt.“ Dann geht sie allein nach Hause."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She laughs, a little. “He used to say that.” Then she goes home alone."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Se ríe, un poco. «Eso decía él.» Luego se va a casa sola."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Elle rit, un peu. « Il disait toujours ça. » Puis elle rentre seule chez elle."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ride, appena. «Lo diceva sempre anche lui.» Poi torna a casa da sola."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "未亡人は少しだけ笑う。「あの人も、よくそう言っていました」。それから、ひとりで家へ帰っていく。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ela ri, um pouco. “Ele vivia dizendo isso.” Depois volta sozinha para casa."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "她笑了，笑得很轻。“他从前也总这么说。”然后她独自回家去了。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_garden.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_garden (widow): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, mein Mann hatte einen Garten beim ersten Haus. Seit er tot ist, wachsen dort Brennnesseln. Ich bin zu alt zum Graben, aber die Kinder würden helfen, wenn ihnen jemand Samen gäbe und einen Grund."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, my husband kept a garden by the first house. Since he passed, it has gone to nettles. I am too old to dig, but the children would help if someone gave them seeds and a reason."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, mi marido cuidaba un huerto junto a la primera casa. Desde que murió, se ha llenado de ortigas. Yo ya soy muy vieja para cavar, pero los niños ayudarían si alguien les diera semillas y un motivo."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, mon mari tenait un jardin près de la première maison. Depuis qu’il est parti, les orties l’ont envahi. Je suis trop vieille pour bêcher, mais les enfants aideraient si quelqu’un leur donnait des graines et une raison."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, mio marito teneva un orto accanto alla prima casa. Da quando se n’è andato, è pieno di ortiche. Sono troppo vecchia per vangare, ma i bambini darebbero una mano se qualcuno desse loro dei semi e un motivo."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、夫は一番目の家のそばに畑を持っておりました。夫が亡くなってから、いらくさだらけです。私はもう掘るには年を取りすぎましたが、誰かが種と理由をくれたら、子どもたちが手伝ってくれるでしょう。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, o meu marido cuidava de uma horta junto à primeira casa. Desde que ele se foi, virou um urtigal. Estou velha demais para cavar, mas as crianças ajudariam se alguém lhes desse sementes e um motivo."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我丈夫在第一座房子边上种过一个园子。他走后，园子里长满了荨麻。我老得挖不动了，可要是有人给孩子们种子和一个理由，他们会帮忙的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Den Witwenpfennig zahlen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pay the widow’s penny"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagar el óbolo de la viuda"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Payer le denier de la veuve"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagare il soldo della vedova"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "手当てをお払いします"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pagar o tostão da viúva"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "照发抚恤"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Stattdessen ein Platz in der Küche"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A place in the kitchen instead"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mejor, un puesto en la cocina"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Plutôt une place en cuisine"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Piuttosto, un posto in cucina"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "代わりに、台所で働きませんか"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Em vez disso, um lugar na cozinha"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "给她厨房里一份差事吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Alte Versprechen starben mit ihm"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Old promises died with him"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Las promesas viejas murieron con él"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ces promesses sont mortes avec lui"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le vecchie promesse sono morte con lui"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "古い約束は、ご主人とともに終わりました"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Promessas antigas morreram com ele"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "旧日的承诺，已随他去了"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Alte Versprechen kosten wenig und kaufen viel Treue auf den Mauern. Zahlt ihr den Pfennig."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Old promises cost little and buy a great deal of loyalty on the walls. Pay her."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Las promesas viejas cuestan poco y compran mucha lealtad en las murallas. Páguele."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Les vieilles promesses coûtent peu et achètent beaucoup de loyauté sur les murailles. Payez-la."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Le vecchie promesse costano poco e comprano molta lealtà sulle mura. Pagatela."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "古い約束は安くつき、城壁の上で多くの忠誠を買います。払い続けるべきです。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Promessas antigas custam pouco e compram muita lealdade nas muralhas. Pague a ela."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "旧承诺花不了多少，却能在城墙上换来许多忠心。照付吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sie nimmt die Münzen mit beiden Händen. Am Abend weiß jede Soldatenfrau, dass {der neue Herr|die neue Herrin} alte Versprechen hält."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She takes the coins in both hands. By evening every soldier’s wife knows the new {lord|lady} keeps old promises."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Toma las monedas con las dos manos. Al anochecer, todas las mujeres de soldado saben que {el nuevo señor|la nueva señora} cumple las promesas viejas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Elle prend les pièces à deux mains. Le soir, chaque femme de soldat sait que {le nouveau seigneur|la nouvelle dame} tient les vieilles promesses."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Prende le monete con tutte e due le mani. Entro sera ogni moglie di soldato sa che {il nuovo signore|la nuova signora} mantiene le vecchie promesse."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "未亡人は両手で硬貨を受け取る。夕方には兵の妻たちの誰もが、新しい城主は古い約束を守ると知っている。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ela recebe as moedas com as duas mãos. À noitinha, toda mulher de soldado sabe que {o novo senhor|a nova senhora} cumpre promessas antigas."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "她双手接过钱币。到傍晚，每个士兵的妻子都知道了，新城主信守旧诺。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tamsin lässt sie Rüben schälen und reden. Beim Abendessen sind sie beste Freundinnen und haben drei Rufe ruiniert."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tamsin puts her to peeling turnips and talking. By supper they are best friends and have ruined three reputations."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tamsin la pone a pelar nabos y a charlar. A la hora de cenar son íntimas amigas y han arruinado tres reputaciones."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tamsin la met à éplucher des navets et à bavarder. Au souper, elles sont les meilleures amies du monde et ont ruiné trois réputations."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tamsin la mette a pelare rape e a chiacchierare. All’ora di cena sono amiche per la pelle e hanno rovinato tre reputazioni."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "タムシンは彼女に蕪の皮むきとおしゃべりをさせる。夕食までに二人は無二の親友になり、三人の評判をつぶしている。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tamsin a põe para descascar nabos e conversar. Na hora da ceia, já são melhores amigas e arruinaram três reputações."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "塔姆辛让她削萝卜、聊天。到吃晚饭时，两人已成了最好的朋友，还毁了三个人的名声。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sie nickt langsam und geht. In der Wachstube verstummen einige der älteren Männer, wenn Ihr vorbeikommt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "She nods slowly and leaves. In the guardroom, some of the older men stop talking when you pass."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Asiente despacio y se va. En el cuerpo de guardia, algunos de los veteranos se callan cuando usted pasa."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Elle hoche lentement la tête et s’en va. Dans la salle des gardes, certains des plus anciens se taisent quand vous passez."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Annuisce lentamente e se ne va. Nel corpo di guardia alcuni degli uomini più anziani smettono di parlare quando passate."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "未亡人はゆっくりうなずいて去る。衛兵詰め所では、年かさの男たちの何人かが、そばを通ると話をやめる。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ela assente devagar e sai. Na sala da guarda, alguns dos homens mais velhos se calam quando você passa."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "她缓缓点头，走了。卫兵室里，有几个年长的兵在你经过时住了口。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.widow_pension.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition widow_pension (widow): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, mein Mann hielt die äußere Linie für Burgherr Aldric und starb dort. Die Zählung führt seinen Namen, und sein Laternenhaken in der Kapelle ist leer. Der alte Herr zahlte mir jeden Monat einen Witwenpfennig. Das Haus seither nicht. Ich verlange, was versprochen war."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, my husband held the outer line for Lord Aldric and died there. The Count has his name, and his lantern’s hook in the chapel hangs empty. The old lord paid me a widow’s penny each month. The house has not. I ask what was promised."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, mi marido defendió la línea exterior por lord Aldric y allí murió. El Recuento tiene su nombre, y el gancho de su farol cuelga vacío en la capilla. El viejo señor me pagaba cada mes el óbolo de la viuda. La casa ya no. Pido lo que se prometió."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, mon mari a tenu la ligne extérieure pour le seigneur Aldric, et il y est mort. Le Compte porte son nom, et le crochet de sa lanterne pend vide à la chapelle. L’ancien seigneur me versait chaque mois le denier de la veuve. La maison, non. Je demande ce qui a été promis."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, mio marito ha tenuto la linea esterna per Lord Aldric ed è morto lì. La Conta porta il suo nome, e in cappella il gancio della sua lanterna è vuoto. Il vecchio signore mi dava ogni mese il soldo della vedova. La casata, da allora, no. Chiedo ciò che era stato promesso."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、夫はアルドリック様のために外の防衛線を守り、そこで死にました。灯数えには夫の名があり、礼拝堂のランタンの鉤は空いたままです。先代の城主様は、毎月、未亡人の手当てを下さいました。今のお城は下さいません。約束されたものをお願いしに来ました。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, o meu marido defendeu a linha externa pelo Lorde Aldric e morreu lá. A Contagem guarda o nome dele, e o gancho da lanterna dele na capela está vazio. O velho senhor me pagava todo mês o tostão da viúva. A casa não pagou mais. Peço o que foi prometido."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我丈夫为奥德里克大人守外防线，死在了那里。数灯的名册上有他的名字，礼拜堂里他那盏提灯的钩子空着。老城主每月发我一份抚恤。兰腾家此后再没给过。我只求兑现当初的承诺。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.c1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dann sei unser Lampenkind"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Be our lamp-runner, then"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Serás nuestro recadero de las lámparas"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sois notre porte-lampe, alors"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Allora sarai il nostro portalampade"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "じゃあ、灯り運びになってね"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Seja o nosso pequeno carregador de lampiões"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "那就来给我们送灯吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.c2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Frag in fünf Jahren wieder"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In five years, ask again"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pregúntamelo dentro de cinco años"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Redemande-moi dans cinq ans"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Richiedimelo tra cinque anni"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "五年たったら、また来てね"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Pergunte de novo daqui a cinco anos"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "五年后再来问我吧"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.c3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Deine Mutter erfährt davon"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your mother will hear of this"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tu madre se va a enterar"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ta mère en entendra parler"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tua madre lo verrà a sapere"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "お母さんに話しておくよ"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A sua mãe vai ficar sabendo disso"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "我会告诉你娘的"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.hint" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: Odile's counsel.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Kinder auf den Mauern sind eine Schande. Kinder, die Feuerschalen neu entzünden, sind ein Gewinn. Macht ein Lampenkind daraus."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Children on the walls are a disgrace. Children who relight braziers are a bargain. Make it a lamp-runner."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Niños en las murallas son una vergüenza. Niños que vuelven a encender braseros son una ganga. Hágalo recadero de las lámparas."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Des enfants sur les murailles, c’est une honte. Des enfants qui rallument les braseros, c’est une aubaine. Faites-en un porte-lampe."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "I bambini sulle mura sono una vergogna. I bambini che riaccendono i bracieri sono un affare. Fatene un portalampade."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもを城壁に立たせるのは恥。篝火を灯し直す子どもは掘り出し物。灯り運びになさいませ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Criança na muralha é uma vergonha. Criança que reacende braseiro é uma pechincha. Que seja o nosso pequeno carregador de lampiões."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "让孩子上城墙是耻辱。让孩子去重新点燃火盆，是划算的买卖。让这孩子去送灯吧。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.r1" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: reaction to choice 1.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "In dieser Nacht huscht eine kleine Gestalt mit einem Kienspan zwischen den Feuerschalen umher und entzündet jede neu, die die Krähen löschen."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "That night a small figure darts between the braziers with a taper, relighting every one the crows put out."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Esa noche, una figura pequeña corre entre los braseros con una tea, volviendo a encender cada uno que apagan los cuervos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cette nuit-là, une petite silhouette file entre les braseros avec une mèche et rallume chacun de ceux que les corneilles éteignent."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quella notte una piccola figura saetta tra i bracieri con un moccolo acceso, e riaccende tutti quelli che le cornacchie spengono."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "その夜、小さな人影が付け木を手に篝火のあいだを駆け回り、烏に消された火を一つ残らず灯し直す。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Naquela noite, uma figurinha corre entre os braseiros com um pavio aceso, reacendendo cada um que os corvos apagam."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "那一夜，一个小小的身影拿着一根火捻，在火盆间穿梭，煤鸦扑灭一个，就重新点燃一个。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.r2" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: reaction to choice 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Kind salutiert feierlich, mit der falschen Hand. Brannock salutiert mit der richtigen zurück, genauso feierlich."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The child salutes solemnly, with the wrong hand. Brannock salutes back with the right one, just as solemnly."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El niño saluda con solemnidad, con la mano equivocada. Brannock le devuelve el saludo con la correcta, igual de solemne."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant salue gravement, de la mauvaise main. Brannock lui rend son salut de la bonne, tout aussi gravement."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino saluta solennemente, con la mano sbagliata. Brannock risponde al saluto con quella giusta, altrettanto solenne."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもは厳かに敬礼する。反対の手で。ブラノックは正しい手で、同じくらい厳かに返礼する。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A criança bate continência, solene, com a mão errada. Brannock responde com a mão certa, com a mesma solenidade."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子郑重地敬了个礼，用错了手。布兰诺克用对的那只手回了礼，一样郑重。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.r3" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit: reaction to choice 3.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Kind wird sehr blass und geht sofort. Manche Drohungen wirken auf jeden Rang."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The child goes very pale and leaves at once. Some threats work on every rank."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El niño se pone muy pálido y se va enseguida. Algunas amenazas funcionan en todos los rangos."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "L’enfant devient tout pâle et file aussitôt. Certaines menaces marchent à tous les grades."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Il bambino diventa pallidissimo e se ne va all’istante. Certe minacce funzionano a ogni grado."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "子どもは真っ青になり、すぐさま出ていく。どんな位にも効く脅しはあるものだ。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A criança fica muito pálida e sai na hora. Certas ameaças funcionam em qualquer patente."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "孩子脸色煞白，立刻溜了。有些威胁，不论官阶高低，一律管用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "petition.young_recruit.text" : {
      "comment" : "Petition young_recruit (child): the request.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Burgherr|Burgherrin}, ich bin fast dreizehn und treffe eine Krähe auf vierzig Schritt mit einem Stein. Hauptmann Brannock hat mich ausgelacht. Lasst mich mit den Schützen auf die Mauer! Ich habe keine Angst. Nur vor meiner Mutter."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "My {lord|lady}, I am almost thirteen and I can hit a crow at forty paces with a stone. Captain Brannock laughed at me. Let me be an archer! I will not be scared. I am only scared of my mother."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mi señor|Mi señora}, casi tengo trece años y le doy a un cuervo a cuarenta pasos con una piedra. El capitán Brannock se rio de mí. ¡Déjeme ser arquero! No tendré miedo. Solo le tengo miedo a mi madre."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Monseigneur|Madame}, j’ai presque treize ans et je touche une corneille à quarante pas avec une pierre. Le capitaine Brannock s’est moqué de moi. Laissez-moi être archer ! Je n’aurai pas peur. Je n’ai peur que de ma mère."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Mio signore|Mia signora}, ho quasi tredici anni e colpisco una cornacchia a quaranta passi con un sasso. Il capitano Brannock mi ha riso in faccia. Fatemi fare l’arciere! Non avrò paura. Ho paura solo di mia madre."
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主様、もうすぐ十三になるよ。四十歩先の烏にだって石を当てられる。ブラノック隊長には笑われたけど。弓兵にして！　怖くなんかない。怖いのはお母さんだけだもん。"
          }
        },
        "pt-BR" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "{Meu senhor|Minha senhora}, eu tenho quase treze anos e acerto um corvo a quarenta passos com uma pedra. O capitão Brannock riu de mim. Me deixe ir para a muralha com os arqueiros! Não vou ter medo. Só tenho medo da minha mãe."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "城主大人，我快十三岁了，四十步外能用石头砸中乌鸦。布兰诺克队长笑话我。让我当弓手吧！我不会害怕的。我只怕我娘。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
